github.com/users/madmmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madmmas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/madmmas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/madmmas/temflowral/commits/16a43838f2ee821e45e4e6e5cf19eb89cc68fd61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-21T11:44:47Z","email":"moinuddinmasud@gmail.com","name":"Moinuddin M Masud"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-21T11:44:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(executor): wait-for-signal node (#58) (#74)\n\n## Summary\n- Adds a contract-first `wait` node (`WaitNodeConfig`: `signal`,\n`timeoutSeconds`) that races a Temporal signal channel against a durable\ntimeout and branches via `received` / `timedOut` source handles.\n- Registers the type in the built-in node registry (`GET /node-types`),\nregenerates Go/TS clients, and covers signal-received vs timeout paths\nin the Temporal testsuite (no HTTP signal endpoint yet — that is #59).\n- Updates README, adding-a-node-type guide, ISSUES/CHANGELOG/DEVLOG.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `make generate`\n- [x] Redocly lint on `api/openapi.yaml`\n- [x] `make test` / `make lint` / `make test-contract`\n- [x] Optional live: after #59, start a graph with a wait node and `POST\n/runs/{id}/signal`; until then Temporal UI / `temporal workflow signal`\ncan exercise a running worker if desired\n- [x] Frontend: palette will show `wait`, but config editor + dual\noutput handles still need UI work (same gap as `condition`)\n\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"e62dce1e1d8f03e14a89fda58cef1c3733049474","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/madmmas/temflowral/git/trees/e62dce1e1d8f03e14a89fda58cef1c3733049474"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/madmmas/temflowral/git/commits/16a43838f2ee821e45e4e6e5cf19eb89cc68fd61","verification":{"payload":"tree e62dce1e1d8f03e14a89fda58