ers/madmmas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/madmmas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/madmmas/temflowral/commits/0ea4bed834e376834de596866499396bf4b91e12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T12:45:59Z","email":"moinuddinmasud@gmail.com","name":"Moinuddin M Masud"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T12:45:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(backend): add durable delay/wait node (#22) (#49)\n\n## Summary\n- add a `delay` node type, defined contract-first as `DelayNodeConfig`\n(`seconds`, 0–604800 = 7 days) and referenced from `Node.config`;\nregenerate Go/TypeScript clients and expose it in the live `/node-types`\nregistry\n- execute the delay inside `GraphWorkflow` via `workflow.Sleep` — a\ndurable Temporal timer that survives worker restarts — instead of an\nactivity, proving durable timers work through the graph translator\n- teach the planner/validator about workflow-handled (non-activity) node\ntypes via `isExecutableNodeType`, and validate delay config at graph\ncreation and plan build (including explicit presence of `seconds`, since\na required non-pointer field would otherwise silently decode to 0)\n- add planner, workflow-timer (asserts a timer actually fires),\nconfig-validation, and registry tests\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Redocly OpenAPI lint\n- [x] generated Go/TypeScript clients refreshed\n- [x] `go vet ./...`\n- [x] `go test -race ./...`\n- [x] golangci-lint v2.12.2 (0 issues)\n- [x] frontend ESLint, Vitest (15/15), production build\n- [x] contract conformance (6/6)\n- [x] Optional manual live check: start Temporal, `make run-backend`,\ncreate a start → delay graph with `config: {\"seconds\": 5}`, run it, and\nconfirm the run stays `running` for ~5s then completes (Temporal Web UI\nat http://localhost:8233 shows the durable timer)\n\nCloses #22\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"5c18335210b24b7cd518046e1b7b6ac21af91a59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/madmmas/temflowral/git/trees/5c18335210b24b7cd518046e1b7b6ac21af91a59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/madmmas/temflowral/git/commits/0ea4bed834e376834de596866499396bf4b91e12","verification":{"payload":"tree 5c18335210b24b7cd518046e1b7b6ac21af91a59\nparent 9259b2f35ed3c2fca214472470725ee95ec66539\nauthor Moinuddin M Masud <moinuddinmasud@gmail.com> 1784465159 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784465159 -0700\n\nfeat(backend): add durable delay/wait node (#22) (#49)\n\n## Summary\n- add a `delay` node type, defined contract-first as `DelayNodeConfig`\n(`seconds`, 0–604800 = 7 days) and referenced from `Node.config`;\nregenerate Go/TypeScript clients and expose it in the live `/node-types`\nregistry\n- execute the delay inside `GraphWorkflow` via `workflow.Sleep` — a\ndurable Temporal timer that survives worker restarts — instead of an\nactivity, proving durable timers work through the graph translator\n- teach the planner/validator about workflow-handled (non-activity) node\ntypes via `isExecutableNodeType`, and validate delay config at graph\ncreation and plan build (including explicit presence of `seconds`, since\na required non-pointer field would otherwise silently decode to 0)\n- add planner, workflow-timer (asserts a timer actually fires),\nconfig-validation, and registry tests\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Redocly OpenAPI lint\n- [x] generated Go/TypeScript clients refreshed\n- [x] `go vet ./...`\n- [x] `go test -race ./...`\n- [x] golangci-lint v2.12.2 (0 issues)\n- [x] frontend ESLint, Vitest (15/15), production build\n- [x] contract conformance (6/6)\n- [x] Optional manual live check: start Temporal, `make run-backend`,\ncreate a start → delay graph with `config: {\"seconds\": 5}`, run it, and\nconfirm the run stays `running` for ~5s then completes (Temporal Web UI\nat http://localhost:8233 shows the durable timer)\n\nCloses #22\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXMcHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvAQQAA/T+iNZGN4G2ZPOl8It3d8F\nzobvM798Wfgpua4h4LwHo36yWRECWohJ4lZRLQhU4p+9a409EMKUPr2jYcYOrueK\noChBl+RmFw4TcIBUk0Jr8WLvi3+meGF58cTR52rwcfCQB0HrXYoGOIB0p4cQrSac\n6vw8lrqQMqYuqfZW9dk07CMInWHYQ8MA5R7kQAwwh43TOzscs4+qeNjpqUPfMveW\nwjS2W5m9yBBksAqu5U/sa/lSWv4p//MRpH6HFK9SXYe/Sfo3DpQLDHJ5CCSNbmi0\nKm4iAyp4or1v8/+N4ROQI5hxSM3ZAUANJUGy7QJqqXO8hII7XDupE5XG887WS/2R\ncVWbQ2O6Yxwg6KPMO+fwxaYJClHMLxVqBHpsKz8fk7MyTWpY18Rxv5KKpI+TbeV6\nTWHpxru1wxHhQapXUmjwaalDh+MQ/kcMkOYhqQl4VyGh7HF0KJ7bmfauL+7YSFOA\nbZAutQ8AjJLBg5rXKuHTESdyO6NWVBUsTcYRETL8a2kFDbj/pHVRCaGsDXi5wBPG\ntiiQS0NZZG9rwpxn673o65g+Dwp/VC7lgPN+GPt2W9qCC2rAGXWGO9Wbs5piSQFL\n0S7cAHN6CcLDiPb8zbddV+i8hNnW7HgRgsrPK9mbA6eXAXPh21Q/xAst/U6L59xm\nD3kRf+vj3dsmHTLiclML\n=8b/N\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-19T12:46:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/madmmas/temflowral/commit/0ea4bed834e376834