ntract): validate API responses against openapi.yaml (#19) (#46)\n\n## Summary\n- Add an AJV-based **contract conformance suite** (`frontend/contract/`)\nthat validates HTTP responses against the exact `api/openapi.yaml`\ncomponent schemas. Validators are derived straight from the spec (via\n`js-yaml` + `ajv`/`ajv-formats`), so there''s no hand-written schema to\ndrift.\n- Covers the success paths for `GET /node-types`, `POST /graphs`, `GET\n/graphs/{id}`, `POST /graphs/{id}/run`, and `GET /runs/{id}`, plus a\nguard test proving the validator rejects a non-conforming payload (so it\ncan''t silently become a no-op).\n- Runs against the **Prism mock by default** (parallel-friendly,\nvalidates the spec''s own examples/schemas + the harness); opt into the\nlive backend with `API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080 npm run\ntest:contract` to catch real drift.\n- Kept in its own `playwright.contract.config.ts` (HTTP-only, no\nbrowser/Next.js), **separate from the UI e2e specs** per the testing\nconventions. Adds `npm run test:contract`, `make test-contract`, and a\n`contract-conformance` CI job gated on api/frontend changes.\n\n## Verification\n- `npm run lint` — clean\n- `npm test -- --run` — 15/15 unit tests pass\n- `npm run test:contract` — 6/6 pass against Prism\n\n## Manual checks\n- **CI:** confirm the new `contract-conformance` job runs and passes on\nthis PR (it should trigger since `api`/`frontend` paths changed).\n- **Dependencies:** review the new dev deps (`ajv`, `ajv-formats`,\n`js-yaml`, `@types/js-yaml`) in `package.json`/`package-lock.json`. The\n2 pre-existing moderate advisories are from `postcss` transitively via\n`next` and are unrelated to this PR.\n- **Optional:** once real backend endpoints exist, run\n`API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080 npm run test:contract` to validate\nthe live implementation against the contract.\n\nCloses #19\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"96d30484f66b81ed087f168c186040dc151e1846","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/madmmas/temflowral/git/trees/96d30484f66b81ed087f168c186040dc151e1846"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/madmmas/temflowral/git/commits/d3938d4c307af0d3fcdb56b237d21c943fb796a9","verification":{"payload":"tree 96d30484f66b81ed087f168c186040dc151e1846\nparent a1b41a6656e0f4cd86a9139ebbd45f553ef1165c\nauthor Moinuddin M Masud <moinuddinmasud@gmail.com> 1784463300 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784463300 -0700\n\ntest(contract): validate API responses against openapi.yaml (#19) (#46)\n\n## Summary\n- Add an AJV-based **contract conformance suite** (`frontend/contract/`)\nthat validates HTTP responses against the exact `api/openapi.yaml`\ncomponent schemas. Validators are derived straight from the spec (via\n`js-yaml` + `ajv`/`ajv-formats`), so there''s no hand-written schema to\ndrift.\n- Covers the success paths for `GET /node-types`, `POST /graphs`, `GET\n/graphs/{id}`, `POST /graphs/{id}/run`, and `GET /runs/{id}`, plus a\nguard test proving the validator rejects a non-conforming payload (so it\ncan''t silently become a no-op).\n- Runs against the **Prism mock by default** (parallel-friendly,\nvalidates the spec''s own examples/schemas + the harness); opt into the\nlive backend with `API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080 npm run\ntest:contract` to catch real drift.\n- Kept in its own `playwright.contract.config.ts` (HTTP-only, no\nbrowser/Next.js), **separate from the UI e2e specs** per the testing\nconventions. Adds `npm run test:contract`, `make test-contract`, and a\n`contract-conformance` CI job gated on api/frontend changes.\n\n## Verification\n- `npm run lint` — clean\n- `npm test -- --run` — 15/15 unit tests pass\n- `npm run test:contract` — 6/6 pass against Prism\n\n## Manual checks\n- **CI:** confirm the new `contract-conformance` job runs and passes on\nthis PR (it should trigger since `api`/`frontend` paths changed).\n- **Dependencies:** review the new dev deps (`ajv`, `ajv-form