"date":"2026-07-19T12:05:56Z","email":"moinuddinmasud@gmail.com","name":"Moinuddin M Masud"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T12:05:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(frontend): scaffold Playwright with Prism (#18) (#45)\n\nCloses #18\n\n## Summary\n- Add Playwright 1.61 with a Chromium project and an isolated\ngraph-editor smoke spec.\n- Start pinned Prism and Next.js automatically; default the frontend API\nURL to Prism.\n- Support `API_BASE_URL` / `PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL` overrides for\npre-existing or real services.\n- Add stable `data-testid` hooks, output ignores, npm/Makefile scripts,\nand usage docs.\n\n## Notes\n- Branch linked to issue #18 via `gh issue develop`.\n- Prism stays a pinned `npx @stoplight/prism-cli@5.14.2` command rather\nthan adding ~185 transitive dev dependencies.\n- The repository''s CI E2E job remains disabled per the testing plan;\nthis scaffold is ready to extend/enable in the dedicated testing track.\n- Do not run `next build` concurrently with Playwright''s managed `next\ndev`; both write `.next`.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `cd frontend && npm test -- --run` (15 tests)\n- [x] `cd frontend && npm run lint`\n- [x] `cd frontend && npm run build`\n- [x] `cd frontend && npm run e2e` (Chromium 1/1; managed Prism + Next)\n- [x] Reviewer: run `npm run e2e:install` once if Chromium is absent,\nthen `npm run e2e`\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"f824e53d927acc384bf34c82ece2d663ecdf74ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/madmmas/temflowral/git/trees/f824e53d927acc384bf34c82ece2d663ecdf74ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/madmmas/temflowral/git/commits/a1b41a6656e0f4cd86a9139ebbd45f553ef1165c","verification":{"payload":"tree f824e53d927acc384bf34c82ece2d663ecdf74ea\nparent 6a88c8ef2eca78b6409035aba8f80b1d1a483871\nauthor Moinuddin M Masud <moinuddinmasud@gmail.com> 1784462756 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784462756 -0700\n\ntest(frontend): scaffold Playwright with Prism (#18) (#45)\n\nCloses #18\n\n## Summary\n- Add Playwright 1.61 with a Chromium project and an isolated\ngraph-editor smoke spec.\n- Start pinned Prism and Next.js automatically; default the frontend API\nURL to Prism.\n- Support `API_BASE_URL` / `PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL` overrides for\npre-existing or real services.\n- Add stable `data-testid` hooks, output ignores, npm/Makefile scripts,\nand usage docs.\n\n## Notes\n- Branch linked to issue #18 via `gh issue develop`.\n- Prism stays a pinned `npx @stoplight/prism-cli@5.14.2` command rather\nthan adding ~185 transitive dev dependencies.\n- The repository''s CI E2E job remains disabled per the testing plan;\nthis scaffold is ready to extend/enable in the dedicated testing track.\n- Do not run `next build` concurrently with Playwright''s managed `next\ndev`; both write `.next`.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `cd frontend && npm test -- --run` (15 tests)\n- [x] `cd frontend && npm run lint`\n- [x] `cd frontend && npm run build`\n- [x] `cd frontend && npm run e2e` (Chromium 1/1; managed Prism + Next)\n- [x] Reviewer: run `npm run e2e:install` once if Chromium is absent,\nthen `npm run e2e`\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXL2kCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjfUQAAkdkmZvRM8EiLn6WQDES9+6\n0b0g41m8oR3fWxuiIiNDtHLkVQeb7+4ay3NZ0Mv6aIKd6dmkVsOwX2rLOoBUOzq8\ngiVWWhmpW9Wpr5IjbEY3pNXp9zb00k57Q85B93+2WFYqwfSjC/wZreoFBpTIV77b\nuM4cMVQTB3utQ7v1QVQeId1+WBsidatWaCXkyIOgIbFYR9rblTDurmOoqxoq7R8b\nCn83WWG+icFMaL/JM/ESnIPGVgZdP0yAiXSpBatDpeGlNdnJlUm6e0rXDADud/MF\n8JwiHtpeiWMY9m+Z6cOUmfSAzG5sbAsnmYE6+6Xul9frBeGqy0tBgqqq1j7m27Hz\nin7ySnOnkphnJbSGgd8Y6sutQVRw66aYZPs7uGRnQ6OFzMho3Dm6C9WJYV9eMVoK\ngOGDZoaMz80DTpLEGMMp8dfxMDScYbbcSNb4HGmLiPz5t6XaoUfq78d4wPb4CU16\nQVgokGphhZzkCJBMl1SSfQG7+4agKx6bIJYgNJsWgvijesvAAMdTb5UjXFXRddO0\n0HGeJ3TKrjhZzpeNAuUMPDf4Wcrompjv5U5p2swa7