T11:36:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(frontend): node palette from node-type registry (#16) (#43)\n\nCloses #16\n\n## Summary\n- Add a `NodePalette` sidebar populated from `GET /node-types` via the\ntyped client (`useNodeTypes`), grouped by category — no hardcoded node\nlist.\n- Add a generic custom `WorkflowNode` renderer (React Flow type\n`workflow`) driven by node data.\n- Wire drag-from-palette and click-to-add so dropping a palette item\ncreates a typed node on the canvas.\n- Extend `createNode` to carry node-type id/label/category; add a pure\n`groupByCategory` helper with tests.\n\n## Notes\n- Branch linked to issue #16 via `gh issue develop`.\n- One data-driven node component instead of a per-type switch;\ntype-specific renderers can be added later without touching canvas code.\n- Palette handles loading/error/empty states gracefully.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `cd frontend && npm test -- --run` (11 tests)\n- [x] `cd frontend && npm run lint`\n- [x] `cd frontend && npm run build`\n- [x] Prism smoke: `/node-types` → 200; dev server compiles and serves\n`/`\n- [x] Manual UX: start Prism (`npx --yes @stoplight/prism-cli@5.14.2\nmock api/openapi.yaml`), run\n`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4010 npm run dev`, and\nconfirm the palette lists node types (Start / HTTP Request), you can\nclick and drag items onto the canvas, connect them, and delete them\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"34b57803f1e9c6009c02c0ba3f4177dc4feb4d7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/madmmas/temflowral/git/trees/34b57803f1e9c6009c02c0ba3f4177dc4feb4d7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/madmmas/temflowral/git/commits/b8f5af1817a440643194ce3e6480ff48b1b37592","verification":{"payload":"tree 34b57803f1e9c6009c02c0ba3f4177dc4feb4d7b\nparent 3f258a368ac01b8e091fd431658f93f7200a59f3\nauthor Moinuddin M Masud <moinuddinmasud@gmail.com> 1784461004 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784461004 -0700\n\nfeat(frontend): node palette from node-type registry (#16) (#43)\n\nCloses #16\n\n## Summary\n- Add a `NodePalette` sidebar populated from `GET /node-types` via the\ntyped client (`useNodeTypes`), grouped by category — no hardcoded node\nlist.\n- Add a generic custom `WorkflowNode` renderer (React Flow type\n`workflow`) driven by node data.\n- Wire drag-from-palette and click-to-add so dropping a palette item\ncreates a typed node on the canvas.\n- Extend `createNode` to carry node-type id/label/category; add a pure\n`groupByCategory` helper with tests.\n\n## Notes\n- Branch linked to issue #16 via `gh issue develop`.\n- One data-driven node component instead of a per-type switch;\ntype-specific renderers can be added later without touching canvas code.\n- Palette handles loading/error/empty states gracefully.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `cd frontend && npm test -- --run` (11 tests)\n- [x] `cd frontend && npm run lint`\n- [x] `cd frontend && npm run build`\n- [x] Prism smoke: `/node-types` → 200; dev server compiles and serves\n`/`\n- [x] Manual UX: start Prism (`npx --yes @stoplight/prism-cli@5.14.2\nmock api/openapi.yaml`), run\n`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4010 npm run dev`, and\nconfirm the palette lists node types (Start / HTTP Request), you can\nclick and drag items onto the canvas, connect them, and delete them\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqXLbMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAqoQABVZ6akInn3je33jm3H/Qre8\nyUGOIDwX05d1SeTPy0wfwmfTvAbUfWDWR66BkSMwAb5mxeT5qLBfiVs+tW1xAuJI\nA/bC4FMz2N4HGl74dKQMGopl0bT7pWMD4i/sFnPnUWr5L46CyWEiNcGd2VL0sPrv\n/AeY90Te1yeGQXHlknDD6pMD3hO0/TQNnX5DXs5aySL/B9RxNIUMId+WHseHXbnq\nG+RGKZITsBMfwox3v2QSk4lzWxgtUtennMJ+ETBrUXz1fBDdPa88BvcpiJct45PG\n9T1EQIFluMfihpRuQmci9mexic2bNBAwW+QLkPc6Ym//hqMB8J1YHTIQ8CgCdcD4\nmz5GSLHBSOSLKYzhUNPPoQ1ZjI1Mlq4oam8jebS08TrHWNXovZAEEKvwGXqtQ