b.com/users/BitResonant/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BitResonant/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BitResonant/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BitResonant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BitResonant/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BitResonant","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BitResonant/SoniChain/commits/a7c36406b8eb0fd578fe5f906f50fdf8699acb9e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T22:22:26Z","email":"matteo.caruso.linardon@gmail.com","name":"BitResonant"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T22:22:26Z","email":"matteo.caruso.linardon@gmail.com","name":"BitResonant"},"message":"Add measured performance notes and engine rationale\n\nExpand README with a new “What it costs to run” section: measured DSP cost (≈3.2% of one core), control-path timings, network-delay dominance, and an observed property of the stream (61.6% zero inter-onset intervals). Clarify design decisions: use a stereo lean (gains 1.0/0.28, 1s glide) instead of hard pan, and document that all three engine banks run continuously (reasoning and measured cost). Update caveats and priorities to close remaining measurement holes and consider tail-based engine release.","tree":{"sha":"f062e649064f7bb03feb66e248ef33872a869c0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BitResonant/SoniChain/git/trees/f062e649064f7bb03feb66e248ef33872a869c0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BitResonant/SoniChain/git/commits/a7c36406b8eb0fd578fe5f906f50fdf8699acb9e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274306202?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BitResonant/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BitResonant/followers","following_u