","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BitResonant/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BitResonant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BitResonant/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BitResonant","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BitResonant/SoniChain/commits/ea38b8d7e0a0a2cf0cd2adc6a183b38e39f35d6c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T21:49:47Z","email":"matteo.caruso.linardon@gmail.com","name":"BitResonant"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T21:49:47Z","email":"matteo.caruso.linardon@gmail.com","name":"BitResonant"},"message":"Refine README: clarify mappings, polish prose, add reverb detail\n\nTighten language for clarity and remove redundancy. Restructure section headings to use colons consistently (e.g., ''Engine A: Glassarmonica'' instead of ''Engine A — Glassarmonica''). Expand the reverb section with explicit RT60 and damping behavior, inverses, and send levels. Clarify that density is an inter-onset interval (not a rate), and that volatility is mapped inversely everywhere for consistency. Remove redundant parameter descriptions already in the mapping table. Delete sonichain-case-study.md, an internal Italian-language planning brief no longer needed.","tree":{"sha":"9e42819ac736084be5a54ed3a5f4714ff1ddfd71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BitResonant/SoniChain/git/trees/9e42819ac736084be5a54ed3a5f4714ff1ddfd71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BitResonant/SoniChain/git/commits/ea38b8d7e0a0a2cf0cd2adc6a183b38e39f35d6c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274306202?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BitResonant/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BitResonant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/u