":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-18T18:34:38Z","email":"mbright@cpacketnetworks.com","name":"Martin-Louis Bright"},"message":"Document macOS launchd install in README\n\nAdd an \"Install as a launchd user agent (macOS)\" section mirroring the\nexisting systemd section: build, install-launchd, configure, start,\ntail logs, restart, and uninstall. Also update the platform note from\n\"Linux-only\" to cover macOS, and add the launchctl restart command to\nthe config-changes note.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"87e9007fadf3273abeca275fcbbd2fd96b37fabe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/git/trees/87e9007fadf3273abeca275fcbbd2fd96b37fabe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/git/commits/9c95f16e887ec9cb444ccfed0a8471a1eed9da6c","verification":{"payload":"tree 87e9007fadf3273abeca275fcbbd2fd96b37fabe\nparent fad951d30d3eece64babdd697d4e11897c58ecf6\nauthor Martin-Louis Bright <mbright@cpacketnetworks.com> 1781807678 -0400\ncommitter Martin-Louis Bright <mbright@cpacketnetworks.com> 1781807678 -0400\n\nDocument macOS launchd install in README\n\nAdd an \"Install as a launchd user agent (macOS)\" section mirroring the\nexisting systemd section: build, install-launchd, configure, start,\ntail logs, restart, and uninstall. Also update the platform note from\n\"Linux-only\" to cover macOS, and add the launchctl restart command to\nthe config-changes note.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3/6C+x0zA56QYYI1srPOTDgVCj\nPE2KY8/Ls7O57qwYYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOuIrv5xEVO9By9lQ2oeOMQtc+LMoWjqjFkNe5q2U9F4X0DiHT6Q5j7pxrSQ8UytQ2\nET8RgxWThaknCaGPgVYgc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-18T20:36:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91706201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mbrightcpacket","id":91706201,"login":"mbrightcpacket","node_id":"U_kgDOBXdTWQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mlbright/ipv6rd/commit/9c95f16e887ec9cb444ccfed0a8471a1eed9da6c","node_id":"C_kwDOS9bfnNoAKDljOTVmMTZlODg3ZWM5Y2I0NDRjY2ZlZDBhODQ3MWExZWVkOWRhNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mlbright/ipv6rd/commit/fad951d30d3eece64babdd697d4e11897c58ecf6","sha":"fad951d30d3eece64babdd697d4e11897c58ecf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/commits/fad951d30d3eece64babdd697d4e11897c58ecf6"}],"sha":"9c95f16e887ec9cb444ccfed0a8471a1eed9da6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/commits/9c95f16e887ec9cb444ccfed0a8471a1eed9da6c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91706201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mbrightcpacket","id":91706201,"login":"mbrightcpacket","node_id":"U_kgDOBXdTWQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/commits/fad951d30d3eece64babdd697d4e11897c58ecf6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-18T17:00:09Z","email":"mbright@cpacketnetworks.com","name":"Martin-Louis Bright"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-18T17:00:09Z","email":"mbright@cpacketnetworks.com","name":"Martin-Louis Bright"},"message":"Add macOS support: poll-based watcher and launchd user agent\n\nSplit platform-specific address watching into watcher_linux.go\n(rtnetlink AddrSubscribe) and watcher_darwin.go (5s net.Interfaces\npoll), with shared business logic remaining in main.go.\n\nReplace netlink.RouteGet with net.Dial(\"udp6\") for egress address\nselection on both platforms — identical kernel source-address\nselection semantics, no OS-specific API surface.\n\nAdd make install-launchd / uninstall-launchd for macOS: installs a\nlaunchd user agent (~/.Library/LaunchAgents/), a wrapper script that\nsources a 0600 env file for OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN, and scaffolds\n~/.config/ipv6rd/ipv6rd.toml and ipv6rd.env.\n\nUpdate ADR 0001 to document the RouteGet → net.Dial change. Add ADR\n0004 recording the macOS port decisions (polling vs route socket,\nuser agent vs system daemon, wrapper vs plist env vars).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"58a4a96536ec26cd4a715e96373798ab1613d3c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/git/trees/58a4a96536ec26cd4a715e96373798ab1613d3c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/git/commits/fad951d30d3eece64babdd697d4e11897c58ecf6","verification":{"payload":"tree 58a4a96536ec26cd4a715e96373798ab1613d3c7\nparent a82d3a7718364aebecbd757cf7142b1a37a3fd13\nauthor Martin-Louis Bright <mbright@cpacketnetworks.com> 1781802009 -0400\ncommitter Martin-Louis Bright <mbright@cpacketnetworks.com> 1781802009 -0400\n\nAdd macOS support: poll-based watcher and launchd user agent\n\nSplit platform-specific address watching into watcher_linux.go\n(rtnetlink AddrSubscribe) and watcher_darwin.go (5s net.Interfaces\npoll), with shared business logic remaining in main.go.\n\nReplace netlink.RouteGet with net.Dial(\"udp6\") for egress address\nselection on both platforms — identical kernel source-address\nselection semantics, no OS-specific API surface.\n\nAdd make install-launchd / uninstall-launchd for macOS: installs a\nlaunchd user agent (~/.Library/LaunchAgents/), a wrapper script that\nsources a 0600 env file for OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN, and scaffolds\n~/.config/ipv6rd/ipv6rd.toml and ipv6rd.env.\n\nUpdate ADR 0001 to document the RouteGet → net.Dial change. Add ADR\n0004 recording the macOS port decisions (polling vs route socket,\nuser agent vs system daemon, wrapper vs plist env vars).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3/6C+x0zA56QYYI1srPOTDgVCj\nPE2KY8/Ls7O57qwYYAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPzWKBYYhtrpuRuQNIxNYL7zqZW5gsfV6oDW6clP4WDsuUNq8kgewsZNIuY8cw9Z45\nhOixRMLe0z1BF19cwTFAQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-18T20:36:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91706201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mbrightcpacket","id":91706201,"login":"mbrightcpacket","node_id":"U_kgDOBXdTWQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mlbright/ipv6rd/commit/fad951d30d3eece64babdd697d4e11897c58ecf6","node_id":"C_kwDOS9bfnNoAKGZhZDk1MWQzMGQzZWVjZTY0YmFiZGQ2OTdkNGUxMTg5N2M1OGVjZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mlbright/ipv6rd/commit/a82d3a7718364aebecbd757cf7142b1a37a3fd13","sha":"a82d3a7718364aebecbd757cf7142b1a37a3fd13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/commits/a82d3a7718364aebecbd757cf7142b1a37a3fd13"}],"sha":"fad951d30d3eece64babdd697d4e11897c58ecf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/commits/fad951d30d3eece64babdd697d4e11897c58ecf6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91706201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mbrightcpacket","id":91706201,"login":"mbrightcpacket","node_id":"U_kgDOBXdTWQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/commits/a82d3a7718364aebecbd757cf7142b1a37a3fd13/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-18T14:57:05Z","email":"mbright@cpacketnetworks.com","name":"Martin-Louis Bright"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-18T14:57:05Z","email":"mbright@cpacketnetworks.com","name":"Martin-Louis Bright"},"message":"Send a separate SPA packet per access entry\n\nThe fwknop-go SPA message format encodes a single proto/port per\npacket (IP,proto/port), so joining access entries into one request\n(e.g. \"tcp/443,tcp/22,tcp/8888\") fails encryption with \"invalid\nproto/port\". Loop over the configured entries and send one knock\neach instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"87ac0d6928d92d7e66a55c8c7ca7395623706faf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/git/trees/87ac0d6928d92d7e66a55c8c7ca7395623706faf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/git/commits/a82d3a7718364aebecbd757cf7142b1a37a3fd13","verification":{"payload":"tree 87ac0d6928d92d7e66a55c8c7ca7395623706faf\nparent d14538198e2b07e83710ec5348782bd22c9abe9d\nauthor Martin-Louis Bright <mbright@cpacketnetworks.com> 1781794625 +0000\ncommitter Martin-Louis Bright <mbright@cpacketnetworks.com> 1781794625 +0000\n\nSend a separate SPA packet per access entry\n\nThe fwknop-go SPA message format encodes a single proto/port per\npacket (IP,proto/port), so joining access entries into one request\n(e.g. \"tcp/443,tcp/22,tcp/8888\") fails encryption with \"invalid\nproto/port\". Loop over the configured entries and send one knock\neach instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgNTlWw6rJhSeXiEDJD2uj3RWERy\nIBwdtaP2G/eSaXNH8AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNwfI1qCdTwmqXWNOniVXygXZQKhW5ktbyuozXdNaTJcYrwsx095pKDO7oYOFzXDbP\npmwBfZBG+dpLG7HqHwnAs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-18T14:59:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91706201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mbrightcpacket","id":91706201,"login":"mbrightcpacket","node_id":"U_kgDOBXdTWQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mlbright/ipv6rd/commit/a82d3a7718364aebecbd757cf7142b1a37a3fd13","node_id":"C_kwDOS9bfnNoAKGE4MmQzYTc3MTgzNjRhZWJlY2JkNzU3Y2Y3MTQyYjFhMzdhM2ZkMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mlbright/ipv6rd/commit/d14538198e2b07e83710ec5348782bd22c9abe9d","sha":"d14538198e2b07e83710ec5348782bd22c9abe9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/commits/d14538198e2b07e83710ec5348782bd22c9abe9d"}],"sha":"a82d3a7718364aebecbd757cf7142b1a37a3fd13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/commits/a82d3a7718364aebecbd757cf7142b1a37a3fd13"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91706201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mbrightcpacket","id":91706201,"login":"mbrightcpacket","node_id":"U_kgDOBXdTWQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/commits/d14538198e2b07e83710ec5348782bd22c9abe9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-18T14:22:11Z","email":"mbright@cpacketnetworks.com","name":"Martin-Louis Bright"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-18T14:33:57Z","email":"mbright@cpacketnetworks.com","name":"Martin-Louis Bright"},"message":"Configure via a TOML file; drop generic command mode\n\nReplace all CLI flags (except --config) with a single TOML configuration\nfile (default /etc/ipv6rd/ipv6rd.toml). The fwknop access request is now a\nlist of protocol/port combinations, sent as one combined access spec in a\nsingle SPA packet. The 1Password service-account token stays the only input\nfrom outside the file.\n\nGeneric command mode is removed: now that the knock is performed in-process\n(ADR-0002), the only command it ever ran was the fwknop CLI it replaced.\nipv6rd is now fwknop-only, with the probe destination fixed to the SPA target.\n\n- main.go: TOML loader (BurntSushi/toml) with strict decoding, defaults, and\n  validation; drop flags, execAction, and the two-mode branching\n- ipv6rd.toml.example: new commented template\n- ipv6rd.service: ExecStart uses --config; EnvironmentFile carries only the token\n- Makefile: scaffold the /etc/ipv6rd config dir + file (0644) and env file (0600)\n- README/CONTEXT/ADRs: document the redesign (ADR-0003 added, ADR-0002 annotated)\n- remove poke-hole.sh\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f53db17895e0e59f366dbbeec5ff4a7d9c8010e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/git/trees/f53db17895e0e59f366dbbeec5ff4a7d9c8010e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/git/commits/d14538198e2b07e83710ec5348782bd22c9abe9d","verification":{"payload":"tree f53db17895e0e59f366dbbeec5ff4a7d9c8010e8\nparent ce1053843db34f79307a5ae267d206a20cea011a\nauthor Martin-Louis Bright <mbright@cpacketnetworks.com> 1781792531 +0000\ncommitter Martin-Louis Bright <mbright@cpacketnetworks.com> 1781793237 +0000\n\nConfigure via a TOML file; drop generic command mode\n\nReplace all CLI flags (except --config) with a single TOML configuration\nfile (default /etc/ipv6rd/ipv6rd.toml). The fwknop access request is now a\nlist of protocol/port combinations, sent as one combined access spec in a\nsingle SPA packet. The 1Password service-account token stays the only input\nfrom outside the file.\n\nGeneric command mode is removed: now that the knock is performed in-process\n(ADR-0002), the only command it ever ran was the fwknop CLI it replaced.\nipv6rd is now fwknop-only, with the probe destination fixed to the SPA target.\n\n- main.go: TOML loader (BurntSushi/toml) with strict decoding, defaults, and\n  validation; drop flags, execAction, and the two-mode branching\n- ipv6rd.toml.example: new commented template\n- ipv6rd.service: ExecStart uses --config; EnvironmentFile carries only the token\n- Makefile: scaffold the /etc/ipv6rd config dir + file (0644) and env file (0600)\n- README/CONTEXT/ADRs: document the redesign (ADR-0003 added, ADR-0002 annotated)\n- remove poke-hole.sh\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgNTlWw6rJhSeXiEDJD2uj3RWERy\nIBwdtaP2G/eSaXNH8AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKHQ/GfvyW1JojYY0C/9pG90DXYY6xg6IO0EPmg+iyqR/1ttI1E2TCtKemG27W0Xry\n+ste591FeS3LH5L3FFFQA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-18T14:34:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91706201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mbrightcpacket","id":91706201,"login":"mbrightcpacket","node_id":"U_kgDOBXdTWQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mlbright/ipv6rd/commit/d14538198e2b07e83710ec5348782bd22c9abe9d","node_id":"C_kwDOS9bfnNoAKGQxNDUzODE5OGUyYjA3ZTgzNzEwZWM1MzQ4NzgyYmQyMmM5YWJlOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mlbright/ipv6rd/commit/ce1053843db34f79307a5ae267d206a20cea011a","sha":"ce1053843db34f79307a5ae267d206a20cea011a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/commits/ce1053843db34f79307a5ae267d206a20cea011a"}],"sha":"d14538198e2b07e83710ec5348782bd22c9abe9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/commits/d14538198e2b07e83710ec5348782bd22c9abe9d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91706201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mbrightcpacket","id":91706201,"login":"mbrightcpacket","node_id":"U_kgDOBXdTWQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/commits/ce1053843db34f79307a5ae267d206a20cea011a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-17T22:04:50Z","email":"mbright@cpacketnetworks.com","name":"Martin-Louis Bright"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-17T23:22:01Z","email":"mbright@cpacketnetworks.com","name":"Martin-Louis Bright"},"message":"Install systemd service without the Go toolchain\n\nDecouple install-systemd from the build target: it now installs a\nprebuilt binary (PREBUILT, default ./ipv6rd) and errors with guidance if\nit''s missing, so the service can be installed on a host that has make and\nroot but not Go. Bundle the Makefile in the release tarball so an\nunpacked package is self-installing via `make install-systemd`.\n\nDocument the make-based and Go-less tarball install paths in the README.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"38ac55fa9594e97dc70f523b8a40a9a663affab7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/git/trees/38ac55fa9594e97dc70f523b8a40a9a663affab7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlbright/ipv6rd/git/commits/ce1053843db34f79307a5ae267d206a20cea011a","verification":{"payload":"tree 38ac55fa9594e97dc70f523b8a40a9a663affab7\nparent 1b8cd2cb2bb7c64cf400a16263051837915f774c\nauthor Martin-Louis Bright <mbright@cpacketnetworks.com> 1781733890 +0000\ncommitter Martin-Louis Bright <mbright@cpacketnetworks.com> 1781738521 +0000\n\nInstall systemd service without the Go toolchain\n\nDecouple install-systemd from the build target: it now installs a\nprebuilt binary (PREBUILT, default ./ipv6rd) and errors with guidance if\nit''s missing, so the service can be installed on a host that has make and\nroot but not Go. Bundle the Makefile in the release tarball so an\nunpacked package is self-installing via `make install-systemd`.\n\nDocument the make-based and Go-less tarball install paths in the README.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgNTlWw6rJhSeXiEDJD2uj3RWERy\nIBwdtaP2G/eSaXNH8AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQA4xG0wziwpSVcXgj9naklmned38Em3ivDvT10ztokxUT5zUfv5VDI5MUXp4MkpvvX\nBE3FTAulUdsrm74xHA4gs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-17T23:22:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91706201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbrightcpacket/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.co