ml_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/dc87799158210ca9e3601db3529951b74be3fc2d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T04:13:06Z","email":"44068562+Leikoe@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Léo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T04:13:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: reconcile the claims with what the tree actually builds (#25)\n\nA skeptical pass over the theory docs, verifying each law against src/\nrather than taking the prose at its word. The theory held up; the\nreporting had rotted. Three fixes, no source touched.\n\nREADME: the \"What runs today, end to end\" section advertised\n`--example gpt2` and `--example trinity` and hung its two headline\nresults on them. Both have been unbuildable since ac5bdbf (2026-07-17)\nmoved them under examples/attic/, which Cargo never compiled; 4a642f3\nonly deleted source that had already rotted unverified. So the front\npage has shipped dead commands for two weeks. Replaced with llama3_2,\nrun end to end, and one line keeping GPT-2/Trinity as history.\n\nThe perf numbers there are now what ten warm repeats reproduce (~52\ntok/s bf16, ~46 f32), not the best single run. A single fresh-warm run\ngives 15.6 ms/tok and the same binary gives 18.6 after half an hour of\nsustained load — the monotonic thermal degradation\nattention-long-context.md documents. Parity with mlx-lm is stated as\nthe durable claim because it was measured head-to-head in one session,\nwhere both sides throttle together; the absolute figure is given as a\nrange.\n\nAlso `cargo test` -> `cargo test --all-targets` in Run it: the plain\nform silently skips the #[cfg(test)] modules in examples/.\n\nREVIEW: three findings were fixed in the tree but still listed as open,\none of them as \"the highest-priority architectural issue\". KernelSpec\nno longer carries the unread tile/SRAM/register fields (resolved by\ndeletion, leaving fold_sched the single owner of the physical\nschedule); CI exists at .github/workflows/ci.yml; and the claim that\nthe Llama example \"only constructs a graph, does not load weights,\ncompile, or run inference\" is false — it binds 146 tensors zero-copy\nand runs. Original text preserved under each, with the CI entry noting\nthe two things a green check cannot cover: no GPU on the runners, and\n--all-targets being load-bearing.\n\ncost-model-cache-term: its acceptance gate read \"225 pass\", which is a\ndead contract at 273. Pin the failure count, never the total.\n\nVerified unchanged and honest: the purity law (every frontend op name\nin derive/simplify/analyze/cost/grad/ir/plan is inside a comment; the\nreal ones live in nn.rs), 8/8 shapes-contract tests, the Hankel rank\noracle, the +-710 magnitude tiers, the GQA free-axis-repeat law, and\nevery file.rs:line reference spot-checked. 273 tests across 30 suites,\nfmt and clippy clean.\n\nStill open, left deliberately: simplify is not in the pipeline (one\ncall outside its module, in a test) while is_contraction stays a\nsyntactic match, so a GEMM spelled as a 3-input Mul partitions\ndifferently and silently. CRITIQUE 1.4 called it; fixing it changes\npartition behaviour on every graph, so it is a design call, not a\ncleanup.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P55SF4m3Unhue5dGUudt7L\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"964eb398844f7ef3d720705584d95bd7a2b947eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/964eb398844f7ef3d720705584d95bd7a2b947eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/dc87799158210ca9e3601db3529951b74be3fc2d","verification":{"payload":"tree 964eb398844f7ef3d720705584d95bd7a2b947eb\nparent 4a642f36a7c543daa9d956bbd915f0000d499d0a\nauthor Léo <44068562+Leikoe@users.noreply.github.com> 1785643986 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785643986 -0700\n\ndocs: reconcile the claims with what the tree actually builds (#25)\n\nA skeptical pass over the theory docs, verifying each law against src/\nrather than taking the prose at its word. The theory held up; the\nreporting had rotted. Three fixes, no source touched.\n\nREADME: the \"What runs today, end to end\" section advertised\n`--example gpt2` and `--example trinity` and hung its two headline\nresults on them. Both have been unbuildable since ac5bdbf (2026-07-17)\nmoved them under examples/attic/, which Cargo never compiled; 4a642f3\nonly deleted source that had already rotted unverified. So the front\npage has shipped dead commands for two weeks. Replaced with llama3_2,\nrun end to end, and one line keeping GPT-2/Trinity as history.\n\nThe perf numbers there are now what ten warm repeats reproduce (~52\ntok/s bf16, ~46 f32), not the best single run. A single fresh-warm run\ngives 15.6 ms/tok and the same binary gives 18.6 after half an hour of\nsustained load — the monotonic thermal degradation\nattention-long-context.md documents. Parity with mlx-lm is stated as\nthe durable claim because it was measured head-to-head in one session,\nwhere both sides throttle together; the absolute figure is given as a\nrange.\n\nAlso `cargo test` -> `cargo test --all-targets` in Run it: the plain\nform silently skips the #[cfg(test)] modules in examples/.\n\nREVIEW: three findings were fixed in the tree but still listed as open,\none of them as \"the highest-priority architectural issue\". KernelSpec\nno longer carries the unread tile/SRAM/register fields (resolved by\ndeletion, leaving fold_sched the single owner of the physical\nschedule); CI exists at .github/workflows/ci.yml; and the claim that\nthe Llama example \"only constructs a graph, does not load weights,\ncompile, or run inference\" is false — it binds 146 tensors zero-copy\nand runs. Original text preserved under each, with the CI entry noting\nthe two things a green check cannot cover: no GPU on the runners, and\n--all-targets being load-bearing.\n\ncost-model-cache-term: its acceptance gate read \"225 pass\", which is a\ndead contract at 273. Pin the failure count, never the total.\n\nVerified unchanged and honest: the purity law (every frontend op name\nin derive/simplify/analyze/cost/grad/ir/plan is inside a comment; the\nreal ones live in nn.rs), 8/8 shapes-contract tests, the Hankel rank\noracle, the +-710 magnitude tiers, the GQA free-axis-repeat law, and\nevery file.rs:line reference spot-checked. 273 tests across 30 suites,\nfmt and clippy clean.\n\nStill open, left deliberately: simplify is not in the pipeline (one\ncall outside its module, in a test) while is_contraction stays a\nsyntactic match, so a GEMM spelled as a 3-input Mul partitions\ndifferently and silently. CRITIQUE 1.4 called it; fixing it changes\npartition behaviour on every graph, so it is a design call, not a\ncleanup.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P55SF4m3Unhue5dGUudt7L\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbsPSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxzwQAFI4lybar3wVFZbpZMmtEjkC\nIn3t4BvSayfho0T/1iuS3B2w+yqMON1MFytAuTWbOi6gk6tZj3sSGkFXuOP5+MwR\ncdks9D6XleBCZ9W/01q9mcrTLuWU1TM9CukQmJFIu2OsYoK2yB21kO0coZbVlTtV\nT165fWWH7ELFGBzA+TA2g3KFFpsGkzkUyu1gL+/dOxfeXEj+CFZNtPrT78iFnEg6\n5B+dNsz120HhcvtHLO67RG06bTJH1umupIjU/rjbk4YH4Glw6g/V5Ig8hlmmB2g3\nZQJUtDljubEt0fbBHAptIEYX3El6CRLIbkmDdja1tw5o51r3pTE4usmU+Q5hJ9/K\nGsqaqgGdsYUAJxqGagDaS7D530ZBFSNV1USxalg+BRZnAvStDZBzd5qmCyg/