{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/2140867e8f1559838461bb163698fba1e23d1487/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T22:22:38Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T22:22:38Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"audit the core diff: -85 lines, and the chunking win does not reproduce\n\nTwo audits of the src/ half of this branch (the other 1.1k lines are tests,\nprobes and writeups). Core was +260/-40; it is now +175/-125.\n\nTHE CHUNKING GOES. SANIC_COMMIT_CHUNKS was landed on a +3.4% measurement that\nwas ORDER BIAS: my A/B alternated but always ran the baseline first in each\npair, and whichever variant ran first lost. Counterbalanced ABBA on the same\nbinary, 6 runs each: chunks=4 is +0.79% mean, +0.40 tok/s median, against a\nnoise sd of 1.05 and a spread of 3.9 — indistinguishable from zero. An\nindependent 24-run counterbalanced test found 0.18%. Either the win was\nregime-specific and the residual-stream commit dissolved it, or it was never\nthere. Sixty-five lines buying nothing measurable is bloat; deleted.\n\npartition.rs, -24 net and far more concept than lines:\n- shared_body_cuts re-derived the streamed-axis translation by hand, when\n  emit_fold computes `stream_provenance` twelve lines above it — same cone,\n  same axis, memoized, and probing shows the lookup never misses. Four match\n  arms collapse to \"price a Map, else descend\". That duplication was the real\n  architectural smell here.\n- the Body struct was ceremony: built at one site, destructured on the first\n  line of its one consumer. It existed to satisfy clippy''s too_many_arguments,\n  which is not a reason to introduce a type.\n- `!Arc::ptr_eq(node, root)` in the done check: zero hits, ever. Dead.\n- body_edges carried a visited set that count_parents, twenty lines above,\n  solves by using the count itself as the marker; it also took &self and never\n  used it.\n- restored leaf_cuts'' doc comment, which I had orphaned onto my new function by\n  splicing code between a doc and the item it documents.\n\ncost.rs: mem_occupancy is now exactly sustainable_bandwidth/hbm_bandwidth, and\nboth call sites multiplied it straight back out. Two spellings of one law with\na float round trip between them — and h*(c/h) != c for ~17% of clamp values, so\nthe round trip was wobbling the cost model by an ulp. Deleted.\n\ngraph.rs: the import belongs inside the gated module, where the other compile\nimports already live — the #[cfg] and its two comment lines vanish.\n\n278 kernels, f32 342, text byte-identical on both dtypes, 222 tests, fmt +\nclippy clean on host and x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"db76a9cfd696da28830841f381ad09cfdb226b41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/db76a9cfd696da28830841f381ad09cfdb226b41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/2140867e8f1559838461bb163698fba1e23d1487","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/2140867e8f1559838461bb163698fba1e23d1487","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDIxNDA4NjdlOGYxNTU5ODM4NDYxYmIxNjM2OThmYmExZTIzZDE0ODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/737c60dc26df5262be17764b3dffb201dd365a06","sha":"737c60dc26df5262be17764b3dffb201dd365a06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/737c60dc26df5262be17764b3dffb201dd365a06"}],"sha":"2140867e8f1559838461bb163698fba1e23d1487","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/2140867e8f1559838461bb163698fba1e23d1487"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/737c60dc26df5262be17764b3dffb201dd365a06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T21:05:56Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T21:05:56Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"pre-commit hook: run CI''s checks at commit time\n\nTwice today the linux CI leg failed on something a host clippy cannot see:\neverything Metal is cfg''d out there, so live macOS code becomes dead-code and\nunused-import errors under -D warnings. Each round trip cost fourteen minutes.\n\n.githooks/pre-commit runs fmt, host clippy, and clippy for\nx86_64-unknown-linux-gnu — the last is the one that catches it, and it needs no\nlinker because clippy only checks. 3.5s warm. `cargo test` is deliberately left\nout: the Metal suite is ~11 minutes, a pre-push cost at best.\n\nVerified by reintroducing the exact regression: host clippy alone passes, the\nhook exits 101 with 23 errors.\n\nEnable per clone with `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`; README says so\nnext to the test command.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d73f3ee33356470ea5acdb33303a7732ba7123e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/d73f3ee33356470ea5acdb33303a7732ba7123e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/737c60dc26df5262be17764b3dffb201dd365a06","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/737c60dc26df5262be17764b3dffb201dd365a06","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDczN2M2MGRjMjZkZjUyNjJiZTE3NzY0YjNkZmZiMjAxZGQzNjVhMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/6a4754631cce4f3290270676cc312dfb7f9aeed8","sha":"6a4754631cce4f3290270676cc312dfb7f9aeed8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/6a4754631cce4f3290270676cc312dfb7f9aeed8"}],"sha":"737c60dc26df5262be17764b3dffb201dd365a06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/737c60dc26df5262be17764b3dffb201dd365a06"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/6a4754631cce4f3290270676cc312dfb7f9aeed8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T21:00:36Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T21:00:36Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"let the llama example be dead code off macOS\n\nEverything in the file below `main` is unreachable on other targets — `main`\nthere is the stub at the foot of the file — so on the linux CI leg the model\ndefinition is 23 dead-code and unused-import errors under\n`clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`. A file-level `#![cfg(target_os =\n\"macos\")]`, which is what the Metal tests use, would leave the target with no\n`main` at all, so the intent is spelled with cfg_attr instead.\n\nPre-existing, like the graph.rs import before it: the example is untouched by\nthe rest of this branch and main''s own CI has been red for 15+ hours.\n\nVerified by cross-checking rather than by CI round trips (thanks Leo):\n  rustup target add x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\n  cargo clippy --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu --all-targets -- -D warnings\nexits 0 with this commit and 101 with 23 errors without it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3810d658d562e3ba7b2a041055400b3e339663e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/3810d658d562e3ba7b2a041055400b3e339663e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/6a4754631cce4f3290270676cc312dfb7f9aeed8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/6a4754631cce4f3290270676cc312dfb7f9aeed8","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDZhNDc1NDYzMWNjZTRmMzI5MDI3MDY3NmNjMzEyZGZiN2Y5YWVlZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/d4db1c0fa647deaa52c5d5b6b28c9e145eede40e","sha":"d4db1c0fa647deaa52c5d5b6b28c9e145eede40e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/d4db1c0fa647deaa52c5d5b6b28c9e145eede40e"}],"sha":"6a4754631cce4f3290270676cc312dfb7f9aeed8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/6a4754631cce4f3290270676cc312dfb7f9aeed8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/d4db1c0fa647deaa52c5d5b6b28c9e145eede40e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T20:42:43Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T20:42:43Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"gate graph.rs''s compile imports on macOS\n\nCompileError, Program and RunError are used only inside this module''s\n#[cfg(target_os = \"macos\")] half, so off macOS they are unused imports and\n`cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` fails the linux CI leg.\n\nPre-existing on main — main''s own CI has been red on this for 15+ hours, and\ngraph.rs is untouched by the rest of this branch. Fixed here so the branch can\nbe judged on its own checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dcfa9bc9dce13eeaa471e634991e49353566ca55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/dcfa9bc9dce13eeaa471e634991e49353566ca55"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/d4db1c0fa647deaa52c5d5b6b28c9e145eede40e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/d4db1c0fa647deaa52c5d5b6b28c9e145eede40e","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGQ0ZGIxYzBmYTY0N2RlYWE1MmM1ZDViNmIyOGM5ZTE0NWVlZGU0MGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/eb55010e985e0f6d1fb5abe48124f7ac4e607d69","sha":"eb55010e985e0f6d1fb5abe48124f7ac4e607d69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/eb55010e985e0f6d1fb5abe48124f7ac4e607d69"}],"sha":"d4db1c0fa647deaa52c5d5b6b28c9e145eede40e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/d4db1c0fa647deaa52c5d5b6b28c9e145eede40e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/eb55010e985e0f6d1fb5abe48124f7ac4e607d69/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T20:25:21Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T20:25:21Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"cargo fmt\n\nThe linux CI leg runs  before the test and clippy steps, and\nit was failing in 5s on my probe files while macos-metal passed all the way\nthrough. Formatting only; no behaviour change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"87a3a94c5d69dd680a8c75e43aacba4594a27d71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/87a3a94c5d69dd680a8c75e43aacba4594a27d71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/eb55010e985e0f6d1fb5abe48124f7ac4e607d69","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/eb55010e985e0f6d1fb5abe48124f7ac4e607d69","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGViNTUwMTBlOTg1ZTBmNmQxZmI1YWJlNDgxMjRmN2FjNGU2MDdkNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/c476b5dc34c40f314abf46d76df996de4a401b66","sha":"c476b5dc34c40f314abf46d76df996de4a401b66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/c476b5dc34c40f314abf46d76df996de4a401b66"}],"sha":"eb55010e985e0f6d1fb5abe48124f7ac4e607d69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/eb55010e985e0f6d1fb5abe48124f7ac4e607d69"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/c476b5dc34c40f314abf46d76df996de4a401b66/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T19:24:03Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T19:24:03Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"item 2: the residual stream IS materialized now\n\nThe note claiming it never is, and that re-reading beats a materialize round\ntrip, is no longer true and the call was wrong. Both contributions of every\nlayer land in a buffer — the MLP one riding its down-projection GEMM as a free\nepilogue, the attention one as a standalone map — and norms read two buffers\nwhere the deepest read 33.\n\nMeasured interleaved on a quiet machine: bf16 57.8 -> 60.1 tok/s (16.6 -> 15.95\nms/step), f32 49.2 -> 50.7, text byte-identical on both dtypes.\n\nRe-reading only looked cheaper because the re-sum was priced at peak bandwidth;\nthe norm reduce is one threadgroup of 128 threads and sees Little''s law''s floor.\nThe prefill half of the note stands untested and is now the stronger claim,\nsince the mechanism it wanted already exists.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a0cebcf5d8de0d1cc226de21d5d56b3bb6717ca5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/a0cebcf5d8de0d1cc226de21d5d56b3bb6717ca5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/c476b5dc34c40f314abf46d76df996de4a401b66","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/c476b5dc34c40f314abf46d76df996de4a401b66","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGM0NzZiNWRjMzRjNDBmMzE0YWJmNDZkNzZkZjk5NmRlNGE0MDFiNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/44e754603b44f017dc3845c3dd229ac9a2abdbaa","sha":"44e754603b44f017dc3845c3dd229ac9a2abdbaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/44e754603b44f017dc3845c3dd229ac9a2abdbaa"}],"sha":"c476b5dc34c40f314abf46d76df996de4a401b66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/c476b5dc34c40f314abf46d76df996de4a401b66"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/44e754603b44f017dc3845c3dd229ac9a2abdbaa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T19:12:29Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T19:12:29Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"materialize the residual stream: bf16 59.5 -> 62.4 tok/s, f32 50.1 -> 51.9\n\nsanic never materialized the residual stream: every norm and projection re-added\nthe whole layer history in-register, the deepest norm reading 30+ buffers. The\n0.588 ms that costs is 100% exposed — reconstructing the barrier schedule shows\nnot one of the 64 norm kernels shares a phase with anything, so there is no\nconcurrent matmul to hide behind. Bytes say it is worth 0.023 ms; the norm\nreduce runs one threadgroup of 128 threads on a 16-core GPU, and that is the 23x\ndifference. This was never a bandwidth optimization.\n\nThe missing piece was a cut POSITION, not a price. leaf_cuts walks downward from\na fold''s leaves, so a value combining several already-materialized leaves lives\nin the body where no walk reaches it. shared_body_cuts walks root->leaves with\nthe same stream translation, in emit_fold, which already does exactly this shape\nof thing. It is priced by the existing Prop 4.1 inequality; sharing is counted as\nparents OUTSIDE this fold''s cone, because a value two slots of one carrier\nreference is emitted once — flash attention''s score contraction has two parents\nand both are the same kernel.\n\nThree defects had to fall with it:\n\nA. shared_body_cuts skipped an already-materialized value instead of reading it,\n   so the residual was stored for exactly ONE consumer and the rest kept\n   re-summing from the links.\nB. the leaf loop then cut a leaf the kernel no longer reaches, emitting a second\n   copy of the down GEMM. Subtree membership is the wrong test: a value the graph\n   reaches another way is still live. reachable_past_cuts walks from the root and\n   stops at cuts, which also subsumes the structural-cut test and lets\n   contains_node — unmemoized, exponential on a DAG — be deleted.\nC. emit_cone emitted the epilogue host via emit, which never consults done, so a\n   host materialized by cutting a sibling cone producer was emitted twice. This\n   one predates the feature: it duplicated a matmul in\n   greedy_decode_step_runs_on_gpu on HEAD.\n\nbf16 263 -> 278 kernels, 15.9 -> 15.4 ms/step. f32 327 -> 342, 19.2 -> 18.7 —\nthere the same disease is cured differently: the score contraction is computed\nonce instead of twice and the exp-sum reads the stored max. Generated text\nbyte-identical to baseline on both dtypes. Same 202 tests pass, clippy clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4c91e28bf057f62f991fd1f817f213d11fafb3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/e4c91e28bf057f62f991fd1f817f213d11fafb3e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/44e754603b44f017dc3845c3dd229ac9a2abdbaa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/44e754603b44f017dc3845c3dd229ac9a2abdbaa","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDQ0ZTc1NDYwM2I0NGYwMTdkYzM4NDVjM2RkMjI5YWM5YTJhYmRiYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/3c34f69fd2c0dc4423ead796a0238857c407a62c","sha":"3c34f69fd2c0dc4423ead796a0238857c407a62c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/3c34f69fd2c0dc4423ead796a0238857c407a62c"}],"sha":"44e754603b44f017dc3845c3dd229ac9a2abdbaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/44e754603b44f017dc3845c3dd229ac9a2abdbaa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/3c34f69fd2c0dc4423ead796a0238857c407a62c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T17:27:44Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T17:27:44Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"the residual regression is one duplicated GEMM per layer, not a verdict\n\nAsked why materializing was slower and measured it instead of explaining it.\nDiffing the two per-kernel profiles puts the entire 3.4 ms in one family: the\nMLP down projection goes 16 -> 31 kernels and its traffic DOUBLES, 538 -> 1042\nMB. Nothing else moves.\n\nThe schedule dump says why. Per layer there are two down-projection folds\nreading the same weight — one carrying the residual add as an EPILOGUE (\"a\nresidual add rides its GEMM for free\", rule 2 of this file, and the baseline\nhas zero epilogues), and one bare. So cutting the residual does light up the\nright path; the bare GEMM just stays live beside it. Cutting every chain link\nrather than the shallowest changes nothing (still 324 kernels), so it is not\nabout which prefixes are stored.\n\nThat makes the verdict OPEN, and the previous commit calling it refuted wrong.\nMy earlier prose explanation — \"the re-sums hide behind the matmuls\" — was a\nstory, and the numbers do not support it: launch overhead for 61 extra kernels\nis ~0.3 ms against a 3.4 ms regression. Item 2''s annotation corrected again to\nsay undecided rather than confirmed.\n\nWhat is measured: position works, cone-aware predicate correct (222 tests,\nflash attention intact), epilogue path engages, integration emits one GEMM\ntwice per layer. Find that and this gets a real answer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"42525abbcf1d429b4e0ec8fad0a8912bcbe98863","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/42525abbcf1d429b4e0ec8fad0a8912bcbe98863"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/3c34f69fd2c0dc4423ead796a0238857c407a62c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/3c34f69fd2c0dc4423ead796a0238857c407a62c","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDNjMzRmNjlmZDJjMGRjNDQyM2VhZDc5NmEwMjM4ODU3YzQwN2E2MmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/a4c5b7872db2014f57a37db1fe7246199b7cd4e3","sha":"a4c5b7872db2014f57a37db1fe7246199b7cd4e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/a4c5b7872db2014f57a37db1fe7246199b7cd4e3"}],"sha":"3c34f69fd2c0dc4423ead796a0238857c407a62c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/3c34f69fd2c0dc4423ead796a0238857c407a62c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/a4c5b7872db2014f57a37db1fe7246199b7cd4e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T17:07:43Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T17:07:43Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"7a: mechanism built and correct, optimization refuted — item 2 was right\n\nBuilt the body-cut position properly this time: one more cut-collection step in\nemit_fold, walking root->leaves with the same stream translation leaf_cuts\nuses. Not in derive — fusing a shared value is legal, so sharing is\nprofitability, and the file''s law is that algebra settles legality while the\ncost model ranks what remains.\n\nThe predicate took two goes. \"More than one parent in the graph\" cuts flash\nattention''s score contraction, whose two parents (max slot, exp slot) are both\nthe same kernel — projected_attention_cuts_the_gemms catches it. What makes a\nrebuild real is a parent in ANOTHER kernel: parents[n] > body_edges[n], edges\ncounted inside this fold''s cone. With that the cuts land exactly on inside=3\ntotal=4 — the residual, read three times in a body and once by the next layer —\nand all 222 tests pass.\n\nThen it loses: 263 -> 324 kernels, 15.9 -> 19.3 ms/step. The 4.78x probe was\nmeasuring norms with nothing beside them; in the real schedule those re-sums\noverlap with the big matmuls and cost nothing to hide, while the extra stages\nand round trip are paid in full. Same regime error as reading SANIC_DEBUG=4\nrates as production — made twice in one day, once with each instrument.\n\nSo item 2''s original call was right and my annotation on it was wrong;\ncorrected in place. The re-sum still grows quadratically with depth, so the\nmechanism is worth keeping for PREFILL, which is what item 2 always said.\n\nMechanism preserved at stash 47bd695. Reverted; 222 tests pass, llama 15.9ms.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"273011d33ec713ce2dc8dd67db7d4399038194ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/273011d33ec713ce2dc8dd67db7d4399038194ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/a4c5b7872db2014f57a37db1fe7246199b7cd4e3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/a4c5b7872db2014f57a37db1fe7246199b7cd4e3","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGE0YzViNzg3MmRiMjAxNGY1N2EzN2RiMWZlNzI0NjE5OWI3Y2Q0ZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/8a7577d964596bdf60fa5df5467efe451e9d630a","sha":"8a7577d964596bdf60fa5df5467efe451e9d630a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/8a7577d964596bdf60fa5df5467efe451e9d630a"}],"sha":"a4c5b7872db2014f57a37db1fe7246199b7cd4e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/a4c5b7872db2014f57a37db1fe7246199b7cd4e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/8a7577d964596bdf60fa5df5467efe451e9d630a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T16:56:30Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T16:56:30Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"7a: two halves landed, and the third''s predicate is measured at the wrong grain\n\nThe architecture was what I had wrong. partition.rs states its own law — the\nderive frontier is the fusion boundary, algebra settles legality and the cost\nmodel ranks what remains. Sharing is not legality (fusing a shared value is\nperfectly legal), so derive must not learn about it; it belongs in emit_fold,\nwhich is already documented as \"cut the carrier leaves the kernel cannot\ncompute in-body, re-plan on the cut graph, push a stage\". One more\ncut-collection step there, walking root->leaves with the same stream\ntranslation leaf_cuts uses. The earlier pre-pass cut BEFORE derivation, which\nis why compile blew to 400s: every fold re-derived from a graph that had moved.\n\nThe body walk works — llama goes 263 -> 391 kernels, so it reaches and cuts the\nresidual chain. Its predicate is wrong: with shared() = \"more than one parent\nin the graph\" it also cuts flash attention''s score contraction, whose two\nparents (the max slot and the exp slot) are BOTH inside the same kernel. The\ncarrier recomputes that in-body on purpose. projected_attention_cuts_the_gemms\ncatches it; 19.3ms confirms it.\n\nWhat makes recompute real is being rebuilt by several KERNELS. A value used\ntwice in one body is emitted once — which is exactly what the count_issue_ops\nfix establishes. The predicate wants parents OUTSIDE this fold''s cone, and the\nwalk already has the cone.\n\nAlso surfaced: materializing changes numerics (boundary storage rounds a bf16\nresidual where an in-register f32 chain did not). Real property to decide, not\nto discover.\n\nReverted to the two landed halves. 222 tests pass, llama unchanged at 15.9ms.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b3893df28d2c947cae5e61cf8e664f06a41775fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/b3893df28d2c947cae5e61cf8e664f06a41775fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/8a7577d964596bdf60fa5df5467efe451e9d630a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/8a7577d964596bdf60fa5df5467efe451e9d630a","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDhhNzU3N2Q5NjQ1OTZiZGY2MGZhNWRmNTQ2N2VmZTQ1MWU5ZDYzMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/4cf195d82f4e04bed0405628d0407c2be68e6cc9","sha":"4cf195d82f4e04bed0405628d0407c2be68e6cc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/4cf195d82f4e04bed0405628d0407c2be68e6cc9"}],"sha":"8a7577d964596bdf60fa5df5467efe451e9d630a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/8a7577d964596bdf60fa5df5467efe451e9d630a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/4cf195d82f4e04bed0405628d0407c2be68e6cc9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T16:33:12Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T16:33:12Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"count each distinct node once in count_issue_ops\n\nIt re-descended every parent edge, which is right for a tree and exponential on\na graph as shared as a transformer''s residual stream: pricing a deep shared\nnode took 200 s on a llama step.\n\nCounting each distinct node once is also the more correct number for a kernel\nBODY, which is what this prices — the emitter names a value and reuses it, so a\nsubexpression two siblings share is issued once inside the kernel, not twice.\n\nllama: same 263 kernels, same text, compile 5.3 -> 4.6 s. 222 tests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"301d1875fa4de3bb523c68d0af7040b2cd5bd728","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/301d1875fa4de3bb523c68d0af7040b2cd5bd728"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/4cf195d82f4e04bed0405628d0407c2be68e6cc9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/4cf195d82f4e04bed0405628d0407c2be68e6cc9","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDRjZjE5NWQ4MmY0ZTA0YmVkMDQwNTYyOGQwNDA3YzJiZTY4ZTZjYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/5eb375624eb056ba987d2a989ec30eec712fa351","sha":"5eb375624eb056ba987d2a989ec30eec712fa351","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/5eb375624eb056ba987d2a989ec30eec712fa351"}],"sha":"4cf195d82f4e04bed0405628d0407c2be68e6cc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/4cf195d82f4e04bed0405628d0407c2be68e6cc9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/5eb375624eb056ba987d2a989ec30eec712fa351/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T16:30:33Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T16:30:33Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"price recompute at the bandwidth a kernel can sustain, not at peak\n\ninline_pays divides both sides of Prop 4.1 by hbm_bandwidth — the rate only a\ngrid wide enough to saturate the machine reaches. A fold whose output is a\nscalar keeps one threadgroup of loads in flight and sees Little''s law''s floor,\n3 GB/s here rather than 200, so re-reading anything into a small fold priced at\n~100ns against a 2us launch: every recompute looked free.\n\ncost::mem_occupancy already IS that law. Stated as the physical quantity a\ncaller wants — sustainable_bandwidth(lanes, bytes in flight) — occupancy\nbecomes its ratio to peak, and inline_pays prices traffic the same way the\nkernel model does.\n\nNo change to llama today (263 kernels, same text, same compile time): the\nresidual stream this was found through is not a fold leaf, so inline_pays never\nprices it. That is a separate missing boundary, next. Landing this on its own\nbecause it is a real mispricing of every leaf cone the partitioner does price.\n\n222 tests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a2422bb6f2e64611f90b4d59ef049b801423721b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/a2422bb6f2e64611f90b4d59ef049b801423721b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/5eb375624eb056ba987d2a989ec30eec712fa351","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/5eb375624eb056ba987d2a989ec30eec712fa351","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDVlYjM3NTYyNGViMDU2YmE5ODdkMmE5ODllYzMwZWVjNzEyZmEzNTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/136b302ccd9c1434c62b86a0db398db9dd10191a","sha":"136b302ccd9c1434c62b86a0db398db9dd10191a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/136b302ccd9c1434c62b86a0db398db9dd10191a"}],"sha":"5eb375624eb056ba987d2a989ec30eec712fa351","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/5eb375624eb056ba987d2a989ec30eec712fa351"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/136b302ccd9c1434c62b86a0db398db9dd10191a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T15:42:17Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T15:42:17Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"7a built to the decision point: the pricing works, the wiring does not yet\n\nFour things established, WIP kept at stash 4cf2a61.\n\nThe cut position is a pre-pass at partition entry walking each root BOTTOM-UP\nand pricing every shared Map — bottom-up so a chain materializes once per link\ninstead of once per prefix. Price the SPLICED view, since the raw node charges\nfor work no consumer redoes and does not terminate on a graph this shared.\n\nThe result that matters: price against ATTAINABLE bandwidth, not peak. At\nhbm_bandwidth the residual re-sum costs ~100ns against a 2us launch and never\npays to cut — which is exactly why nothing was hoisting. At the rate a\nscalar-output fold sustains (Little''s law floor, 1/64 of peak, ~3 GB/s here)\nthe same re-sum is tens of us, matching both the measured 6->31us slope and\nthe probe. cost::mem_occupancy already IS that law; it needed factoring out so\na caller holding a lane count can use it. With that, 64 nodes price as worth\nhoisting, in 7s.\n\nAlso found: plan::count_issue_ops is exponential on shared DAGs — it\nre-descends every parent edge, 200s on llama. It is also the wrong count for a\nkernel body, where the emitter names a value once; a memoized walk is linear\nAND more correct. Latent bug on existing callers, not just this pass.\n\nWhat stopped it: with the 64 cuts taken, compile blows past 400s. Dry-run is\nfast, so the cost is in cut->emit re-planning, not pricing — probably cutting\ninside a fold body forces the enclosing fold to re-plan and cascades. A wiring\nproblem, and it wants a fresh session rather than the tail of a long one.\n\nTree reverted, 222 tests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"94e406d5b4a93b4d528a1610fba728554dc0c2e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/94e406d5b4a93b4d528a1610fba728554dc0c2e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/136b302ccd9c1434c62b86a0db398db9dd10191a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/136b302ccd9c1434c62b86a0db398db9dd10191a","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDEzNmIzMDJjY2Q5YzE0MzRjNjJiODZhMGRiMzk4ZGI5ZGQxMDE5MWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/c6cc34279a1af89dc25647b05fdf5d0824f53d24","sha":"c6cc34279a1af89dc25647b05fdf5d0824f53d24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/c6cc34279a1af89dc25647b05fdf5d0824f53d24"}],"sha":"136b302ccd9c1434c62b86a0db398db9dd10191a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/136b302ccd9c1434c62b86a0db398db9dd10191a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/c6cc34279a1af89dc25647b05fdf5d0824f53d24/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T14:56:03Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T14:56:03Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"7a: the blocker is a missing cut POSITION, not a mispriced one\n\nTried the obvious implementation: teach Prop 4.1 that a shared subtree is\nrecomputed once per CONSUMING KERNEL, not just once per replica within one —\nscale `replicas` by the node''s parent count in inline_pays. One line. It\nchanges nothing: still 263 kernels.\n\nInstrumented to find out why, and inline_pays is never called on the residual\nsum at all. The sharing is there in the graph — parent-count histogram over\nllama is {1: 1739, 2: 198, 3: 50, 4: 33, 16: 2, 32: 3, 33: 3, 34: 1, 52: 1},\nand the heavy entries are Map/Add — but leaf_cuts never visits those nodes;\nwhat it does visit at parents >= 4 is already `done`. The layer CONTRIBUTIONS\nare materialized. The Add TREE that combines them is not a fold leaf: it lives\nin the fold''s BODY, and leaf_cuts only walks downward from leaves. There is no\ncut position there for any price to apply to.\n\nSo 7a needs a capability, not a number — hoisting a shared sub-expression out\nof fold bodies into its own stage. That generalizes (it is the same move for\nany shared body expression, so it stays a law rather than a residual-stream\nrule) but it is new partitioner machinery and deserves designing before\npricing. Exploration reverted; the probe and the 0.43 ms stand.\n\n222 tests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1d6eff1dd053dc05157d1b1042209d252307977d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/1d6eff1dd053dc05157d1b1042209d252307977d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/c6cc34279a1af89dc25647b05fdf5d0824f53d24","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/c6cc34279a1af89dc25647b05fdf5d0824f53d24","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGM2Y2MzNDI3OWExYWY4OWRjMjU2NDdiMDVmZGY1ZDA4MjRmNTNkMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/2493d254a6fb63c190077d4efd1beed9658ec235","sha":"2493d254a6fb63c190077d4efd1beed9658ec235","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/2493d254a6fb63c190077d4efd1beed9658ec235"}],"sha":"c6cc34279a1af89dc25647b05fdf5d0824f53d24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/c6cc34279a1af89dc25647b05fdf5d0824f53d24"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/2493d254a6fb63c190077d4efd1beed9658ec235/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T14:34:21Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T14:34:21Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"7a confirmed by probe: materializing the residual wins 4.78x, ~0.43 ms/step\n\nHand-built both shapes at llama''s geometry before touching the partitioner —\n33 norms whose arity grows with depth, against 32 adds plus 33 arity-1 norms:\n\n  re-sum (today)   66 dispatches  1489.7us\n  materialize      98 dispatches   311.7us   4.78x\n\nThe probe''s absolutes run ~1.6x hot against a real step (its norms have no big\nmatmuls beside them to hide behind), so scale by the ratio: real norms cost\n0.951 ms, arity 1 would be 0.363, and 32 adds at the ~5us our other 2048-wide\nmaps take is ~0.16 — 0.951 -> ~0.52, saving ~0.43 ms/step. That lands on the\n0.4 ms this item estimated from the arity slope, by a different route.\n\nWorth naming: the winning shape has THIRTY-TWO MORE DISPATCHES and does less\ntotal work. Every fusion this project has tried lost by trading away threads\nor arithmetic; this is the first item where the fix is to stop fusing.\n\nNot built — it is a cost-model change (the model currently prices a re-read\nbelow a materialize round-trip) and deserves its own session. Pinned by an\nassertion that fails if re-summing ever wins.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4be385072d4a2674c9b96006e190ec0deef1d2f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/4be385072d4a2674c9b96006e190ec0deef1d2f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/2493d254a6fb63c190077d4efd1beed9658ec235","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/2493d254a6fb63c190077d4efd1beed9658ec235","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDI0OTNkMjU0YTZmYjYzYzE5MDA3N2Q0ZWZkMWJlZWQ5NjU4ZWMyMzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/a669a2992b1a9517dfb11326e66f5e04639ed8e6","sha":"a669a2992b1a9517dfb11326e66f5e04639ed8e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/a669a2992b1a9517dfb11326e66f5e04639ed8e6"}],"sha":"2493d254a6fb63c190077d4efd1beed9658ec235","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/2493d254a6fb63c190077d4efd1beed9658ec235"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/a669a2992b1a9517dfb11326e66f5e04639ed8e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T14:29:58Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T14:29:58Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"7e LANDED: commit the replay in chunks so the GPU starts before encoding ends\n\nA step encoded into one command buffer cannot start on the GPU until the host\nhas finished encoding all 263 dispatches. replay_checked now commits in\nchunks, so chunk k runs while k+1 is still being encoded. Command buffers on\none queue execute in commit order, so a chunk boundary is itself a barrier and\nthe capture-time schedule still holds; run_graph_timed spans the first\nbuffer''s GPUStartTime to the last''s GPUEndTime so the reported figure still\ncovers the whole step, and every chunk''s error is checked.\n\nMeasured, llama-3.2-1B bf16, 128 tokens, decode tok/s:\n\n  1 -> 55.5   2 -> 56.0   4 -> 57.4   8 -> 57.3   16 -> 56.8   32 -> 55.6\n\nDefault 4, ~0.6 ms/step, +3.4% — the same curve shape and the same optimum\nMLX''s own commit policy sweeps out. 221 tests pass; generated text unchanged\non both the bf16 and f32 paths.\n\nWorth less than the ~1 ms first estimated, and the reason is instructive: that\nfigure priced MLX''s chopping with MLX''s caps, but MLX is eager and pays a\nlarge per-dispatch host cost while sanic replays a frozen graph. Only the\nENCODE part of the host gap can be hidden, and ours is small.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2f500a98c9c653bf0ec219b53ffca6d0d489eadc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/2f500a98c9c653bf0ec219b53ffca6d0d489eadc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/a669a2992b1a9517dfb11326e66f5e04639ed8e6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/a669a2992b1a9517dfb11326e66f5e04639ed8e6","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGE2NjlhMjk5MmIxYTk1MTdkZmIxMTMyNmU2NmY1ZTA0NjM5ZWQ4ZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/dbaa4f42e36d9dcf44896f00c42b28726f64d1a8","sha":"dbaa4f42e36d9dcf44896f00c42b28726f64d1a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/dbaa4f42e36d9dcf44896f00c42b28726f64d1a8"}],"sha":"a669a2992b1a9517dfb11326e66f5e04639ed8e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/a669a2992b1a9517dfb11326e66f5e04639ed8e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/dbaa4f42e36d9dcf44896f00c42b28726f64d1a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T14:22:00Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T14:22:00Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"7b refuted, and item 4 was right about the kernels — the slack was my regime error\n\nHand-probed the emitted matvec fold against uint4 (16-byte) and uint2 (8-byte)\nrewrites of the same sweep, 8 dispatches over 8 distinct cold weights in one\ncommand buffer:\n\n  gate/up 2048->8192, 8192 tgs:  scalar 183.6  uint2 185.6  uint4 185.0 GB/s\n  down    8192->2048, 2048 tgs:  scalar 167.6  uint4 167.1 GB/s\n\n1.01x and 1.00x. Widening the load instruction is worth nothing; P1 dies\nalongside P2. Pinned by wide_loads_stay_worth_nothing.\n\nThe bigger result is a correction to item 7, and it is mine to own. That item\nread the SANIC_DEBUG=4 per-class table (gate/up 166, down 153 GB/s) as 1.69 ms\nof codegen slack and challenged item 4''s \"the generated kernels are essentially\noptimal\". The probe measures the same shapes at 183.6 and 167.6 back-to-back:\n=4 gives every kernel its own encoder and charges it a ramp production hides,\nso I read an isolated-regime number as production — the same class of error I\nhad accused item 4 of making with its aggregate. Item 4 was right. Both\nannotations on it corrected.\n\nWhat survives is narrower and real: down and gate/up run IDENTICAL code at\n167.6 and 183.6 GB/s, differing only in threadgroup count (2048 vs 8192). That\nis grid width, Little''s law, and splitting a narrow-output projection''s\nreduction RAISES thread count — the right side of the block-rows law. Worth\n~0.28 ms on down, ~0.4-0.5 total, not 1.69.\n\n221 tests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9a919ca0d221502f3f8b99f3456995b26265d9bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/9a919ca0d221502f3f8b99f3456995b26265d9bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/dbaa4f42e36d9dcf44896f00c42b28726f64d1a8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/dbaa4f42e36d9dcf44896f00c42b28726f64d1a8","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGRiYWE0ZjQyZTM2ZDlkY2Y0NDg5NmYwMGM0MmIyODcyNmY2NGQxYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/6d570749ffc57ed6b02bb3e1298e67f196df6ec3","sha":"6d570749ffc57ed6b02bb3e1298e67f196df6ec3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/6d570749ffc57ed6b02bb3e1298e67f196df6ec3"}],"sha":"dbaa4f42e36d9dcf44896f00c42b28726f64d1a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/dbaa4f42e36d9dcf44896f00c42b28726f64d1a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/6d570749ffc57ed6b02bb3e1298e67f196df6ec3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T06:32:29Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T06:32:29Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"7c built, measured, refuted: a saturating grid leaves no slots for a neighbour\n\nBuilt the reorder — sort dispatches by dependency depth over the same\nRAW/WAW/WAR relation on the same allocation identity barrier_schedule uses,\nwhich preserves every ordering that carries data. It worked exactly as\ndesigned: 263 dispatches went 213 phases -> 180, the DAG floor, with q, k\nand v sharing a phase in 15 of 16 layers, and all 218 tests passed through\nthe reordered path.\n\nIt bought nothing. Five A/B pairs in one session, level order never once\nfaster and ~0.14 ms consistently worse:\n\n  level order (180 phases): 16.6 16.6 16.4 16.6 16.4 ms\n  emission order (213):     16.4 16.4 16.4 16.3 16.4 ms\n\nReverted — 45 lines that buy nothing are not worth their weight.\n\nWhy, and it is the useful part: a grid that already fills the machine leaves\nno slots for a concurrent neighbour. The q projection is ~65k threads on a\n16-core GPU, so k and v queue behind it barrier or no barrier. Concurrency\npays only where grids are small, and small grids are 8.8% of kernel time —\nthe block-rows law seen from the other end.\n\nTwo consequences. The 1.68 ms barriers=none gap is not legal-concurrency-\nshaped, so item 4''s \"the serialization is in the model, not the runtime\" now\nrests on a correct run rather than a racy one, and the 1.69 ms of\nweight-class slack has one door left: 7b, raise the isolated per-kernel\nrate. And merging q/k/v stays open but on a different mechanism — not more\nbytes in flight from concurrency, which is refuted, but one grid large\nenough to saturate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e6328a2dc5c03a326c41ed2056e737ab5416f42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/9e6328a2dc5c03a326c41ed2056e737ab5416f42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/6d570749ffc57ed6b02bb3e1298e67f196df6ec3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/6d570749ffc57ed6b02bb3e1298e67f196df6ec3","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDZkNTcwNzQ5ZmZjNTdlZDZiMDJiYjNlMTI5OGU2N2YxOTZkZjZlYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/2ef5214d7a6355a7d47d492c61370918fe80168e","sha":"2ef5214d7a6355a7d47d492c61370918fe80168e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/2ef5214d7a6355a7d47d492c61370918fe80168e"}],"sha":"6d570749ffc57ed6b02bb3e1298e67f196df6ec3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/6d570749ffc57ed6b02bb3e1298e67f196df6ec3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/2ef5214d7a6355a7d47d492c61370918fe80168e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T06:17:08Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T06:17:08Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"item 7c: q, k and v each sit in a phase ALONE — theory 4 is half wrong\n\nItem 4 dismissed sideways fusion of q|k|v on the arithmetic that 263\ndispatches minus 212 barriers leaves 51 free, so \"those kernels ALREADY run\nconcurrently\". Replayed the emitted barrier schedule and tagged each phase\nby which projection weights it reads: the only projection pair that ever\nshares a phase is gate|up, 16 times, one per layer. q, k and v each sit in a\nphase alone, though the DAG makes them mutually independent — the 31\nwidth-3 levels of the ideal schedule are exactly these.\n\nSo theory 4 holds for gate|up and is untested for q|k|v. Two ways in,\ncheapest first: reorder the three adjacent so one phase covers them (no\nfusion, no new kernel, and the cheapest possible test of the ramp-filling\nhypothesis barriers=none raised), then merge into one [3072, 2048] stream if\nthat pays — which also RAISES thread count, so it sits on the right side of\nthe block-rows law rather than against it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"70ade5833bafb6888ca7c1a148b902c5668b7039","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/70ade5833bafb6888ca7c1a148b902c5668b7039"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/2ef5214d7a6355a7d47d492c61370918fe80168e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/2ef5214d7a6355a7d47d492c61370918fe80168e","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDJlZjUyMTRkN2E2MzU1YTdkNDdkNDkyYzYxMzcwOTE4ZmU4MDE2OGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/f01e6ba71787745762dcdc9693eedcba65c31a12","sha":"f01e6ba71787745762dcdc9693eedcba65c31a12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/f01e6ba71787745762dcdc9693eedcba65c31a12"}],"sha":"2ef5214d7a6355a7d47d492c61370918fe80168e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/2ef5214d7a6355a7d47d492c61370918fe80168e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/f01e6ba71787745762dcdc9693eedcba65c31a12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T06:14:51Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T06:14:51Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"todo item 7: the roofline per class, and the two conclusions that would have blocked it\n\nThe goal is the ROOFLINE — 100% of bandwidth on the traffic we do — not the\nfastest number, so quantization, speculative decoding and batching are out\nof scope by construction: each moves the floor instead of reaching it.\n\nItem 4 read barriers=none at 13.87 ms against a 13.48 traffic floor, called\nit 97% of practical peak, and concluded the kernels are essentially optimal\nand wide-load work is a dead end. A per-class look does not support that.\nSANIC_DEBUG=4 times each kernel in ISOLATION and the rates are not uniform:\nlm_head reaches 184 GB/s with a 128k grid while the MLP folds — same\ncodegen, 8k grid — sit at 153-166, q/o at 151-158, k/v at 120. Weight-class\nslack is 1.69 ms against the 1.68 ms item 4 blames on the serial chain: not\ntwo problems, one problem from two sides. A fold that cannot saturate DRAM\nalone either has its ramp filled by a neighbour (barriers off, aggregate\n97%) or runs below peak in isolation (real schedule, 83-90%). Item 4 closed\nboth doors; at most one could be shut.\n\nFive items in measured value order: materialize the residual (~0.4 ms, and\nit corrects item 2''s untimed \"re-reading beats a materialize round-trip\" —\nthe re-sum costs 0.588 ms and grows quadratically with depth), wide loads on\nthe MLP folds (~1.2), merge q/k/v (~0.19), fuse the small ops into the\nstreams they ride (up to 1.43, and sanic already emits the mechanism at\nlayer 0), pipeline submission (~1 ms, host side).\n\nBoth superseded conclusions annotated in place so neither gets cited to skip\nthis. Cross-check that it is not sanic-specific: mlx-lm reconstructs to\n16.42 ms on the same traffic, 76% of roofline against our 75%.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b671e14b8691825c702666ec4ee3283eceb36a9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/b671e14b8691825c702666ec4ee3283eceb36a9f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/f01e6ba71787745762dcdc9693eedcba65c31a12","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/f01e6ba71787745762dcdc9693eedcba65c31a12","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGYwMWU2YmE3MTc4Nzc0NTc2MmRjZGM5NjkzZWVkY2JhNjVjMzFhMTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/3db4639029c72ad08a2d3447deeae7019ae90316","sha":"3db4639029c72ad08a2d3447deeae7019ae90316","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/3db4639029c72ad08a2d3447deeae7019ae90316"}],"sha":"f01e6ba71787745762dcdc9693eedcba65c31a12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/f01e6ba71787745762dcdc9693eedcba65c31a12"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/3db4639029c72ad08a2d3447deeae7019ae90316/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T06:04:47Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T06:04:47Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"the norm gap is the re-sum, not the split — and the old probe never left arity 1\n\nDecomposed the 0.95 vs 0.21 ms norm gap. The obvious suspect, our 66\ndispatches against fast.rms_norm''s 33, is the wrong one, and this repo had\nalready measured that: fused_rms_against_reduce_then_apply times a\nhand-written fused two-pass kernel at 7.71 us against reduce+apply''s 8.00 —\n1.04x, ~9 us/step, 0.06%. Fusing the split is worth nothing.\n\nBut that probe runs at arity ONE, and never left it. In the real step the\nnorms are not arity one: with the residual stream never materialized, each\nnorm re-sums every prior layer, reduce climbing 6 -> 31 us and apply 5 -> 12\nwhile the k/v folds beside them stay flat at ~17. Holding arity at 1 the\nnorms would cost 0.363 ms instead of 0.951 — so 0.588 ms of the 0.75 ms gap\nis the re-sum, arithmetic and loads, and no fusion of the two dispatches\nremoves a single Add of it.\n\nThe lever is materialization, not fusion: writing the residual once per\nlayer buys the 0.588 ms for ~32 small adds (~0.16 ms by analogy with our\nother 2048-wide maps), a net ~0.4 ms/step. Estimated from measured\nneighbours, not measured — but it contradicts the standing note in todo.md\n2 that \"at batch-1 decode re-reading k*4KB beats a materialize round-trip\",\nwhich was reasoned rather than timed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ae867db37e71438b297e04bfb7965db731d5bd30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/ae867db37e71438b297e04bfb7965db731d5bd30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/3db4639029c72ad08a2d3447deeae7019ae90316","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/3db4639029c72ad08a2d3447deeae7019ae90316","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDNkYjQ2MzkwMjljNzJhZDA4YTJkMzQ0N2RlZWFlNzAxOWFlOTAzMTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/c5970763123d3cc088ac6650d86afd230151b641","sha":"c5970763123d3cc088ac6650d86afd230151b641","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/c5970763123d3cc088ac6650d86afd230151b641"}],"sha":"3db4639029c72ad08a2d3447deeae7019ae90316","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/3db4639029c72ad08a2d3447deeae7019ae90316"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/c5970763123d3cc088ac6650d86afd230151b641/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T05:57:09Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T05:57:09Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"correction: the boundaries COINCIDE — norm-into-projection was 2 of 32, not 32\n\nChecked the previous commit''s fusion claims against the emitted MSL instead\nof the schedule dump''s tags, and one of the three was wrong.\n\nnorm-into-projection is NOT a model-wide fusion: only layer 0''s k and v fuse\nit (as a deferred-division tuple fold). The other 30 projections, and every\nq and gate/up, read a materialized normalized input — the same shape MLX\nhas. So the k/v class winning 0.56 ms against 0.86 is the fold beating the\ngemv, not a fusion the other engine lacks.\n\nThe other two hold, now counted: RoPE fuses into the k cache write in 16 of\n16 layers (the v half is a plain scatter in both engines), and all 32\nresidual adds are absorbed model-wide — 1,863 of sanic''s 3,193 algebra ops\nare Add, and the norm folds grow by exactly two adds per layer (1, 3, 5, …,\n65).\n\nWhich makes the honest headline the opposite of the earlier one: the kernel\nboundaries largely COINCIDE. A primitive library is already a fused kernel\nset (rms_norm.metal reduces and applies in one dispatch behind threadgroup\nbarriers; sdpa is one online-softmax kernel; mx.compile folds the SiLU\nchain), so \"we fuse, they don''t\" is false. Both cut where a contraction\nforces materialization — MLX by hand once, sanic per graph from the\ncriterion — and the counts agree class by class. Exactly three boundaries\ndiffer, and all three are where the time differs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5cdc9e2b05d6c944a645236f9a9eb936b79b0d5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/5cdc9e2b05d6c944a645236f9a9eb936b79b0d5c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/c5970763123d3cc088ac6650d86afd230151b641","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/c5970763123d3cc088ac6650d86afd230151b641","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGM1OTcwNzYzMTIzZDNjYzA4OGFjNjY1MGQ4NmFmZDIzMDE1MWI2NDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/9aab19c1fac7610bc47361da5e38ec62171817bb","sha":"9aab19c1fac7610bc47361da5e38ec62171817bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/9aab19c1fac7610bc47361da5e38ec62171817bb"}],"sha":"c5970763123d3cc088ac6650d86afd230151b641","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/c5970763123d3cc088ac6650d86afd230151b641"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/9aab19c1fac7610bc47361da5e38ec62171817bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T05:50:49Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T05:50:49Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"the kernels inside those schedules: within 2%, and the folds are not the weak side\n\nPer-class comparison of what sanic emits against what mlx-lm dispatches, one\nllama-3.2-1B bf16 decode step. sanic''s side is SANIC_DEBUG=4 in-graph\ntimestamps (16.57 ms over 263 kernels); MLX''s is per-class microbenchmarks\nat the census counts.\n\nOne methodological correction carries the result: benchmarking a projection\n200x leaves its weight SLC-resident and reports 303 GB/s, above this\nmachine''s DRAM peak. Allocating one DISTINCT weight per dispatch reproduces\nthe step''s 2.47 GB ledger, and the reconstructed total then lands at\n16.42 ms against mlx-lm''s measured 16.2-16.9 — the parts add up to the wall.\n\nKernel for kernel the engines are within 2% (16.57 vs 16.42). The derived\none-thread-per-output matvec fold BEATS MLX''s hand-written gemv on every\nattention projection (1.2-1.5x) and on lm_head; MLX keeps ~5% on the two big\nMLP classes. Three fusions have no MLX counterpart: norm-into-projection,\nRoPE-into-cache-write, and all 32 residual Adds deleted.\n\nThat last one is also the single clear loss. RMS norms cost 0.96 ms against\nMLX''s 0.21 — the norm is split into reduce+apply (66 dispatches vs 33), and\nbecause the residual stream is never materialized each norm re-sums every\nprior layer: measured 6us at layer 0 climbing to 29us at layer 15, while the\nk/v folds beside them stay flat at ~17us. The 32 saved Adds (0.10 ms) do not\ncover the ~0.7 ms of growth, and the re-sum is quadratic in depth. todo.md\nflagged this shape for prefill; this is the decode price.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ff51dbfaf583c04cd8b01ba39458af813f7ff640","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/ff51dbfaf583c04cd8b01ba39458af813f7ff640"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/9aab19c1fac7610bc47361da5e38ec62171817bb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/9aab19c1fac7610bc47361da5e38ec62171817bb","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDlhYWIxOWMxZmFjNzYxMGJjNDczNjFkYTVlMzhlYzYyMTcxODE3YmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/f2d2d664a685628c818d96a0d2f4f5ddfdf30fb2","sha":"f2d2d664a685628c818d96a0d2f4f5ddfdf30fb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/f2d2d664a685628c818d96a0d2f4f5ddfdf30fb2"}],"sha":"9aab19c1fac7610bc47361da5e38ec62171817bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/9aab19c1fac7610bc47361da5e38ec62171817bb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/f2d2d664a685628c818d96a0d2f4f5ddfdf30fb2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T05:38:59Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T05:38:59Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"the two schedules are the same schedule — the gap is when work is submitted\n\nCompared sanic''s dispatch list against mlx-lm''s primitive graph on one\nllama-3.2-1B bf16 decode step, both measured, not argued.\n\nThey match: 263 launches vs 276, dependency depth 180 vs 196, available\nwidth 1.46 vs 1.41 — and the barrier LAW is identical (accumulate accesses,\nbarrier on RAW/WAW/WAR against allocation identity, reset), arrived at\nindependently; sanic computes it once at capture, MLX rediscovers it per\ndispatch because it is eager. 535 of MLX''s 811 graph nodes are view\nrewrites sanic never materializes at all.\n\nThe difference is submission granularity. MLX''s byte cap (40 mega-ELEMENTS\nof distinct inputs, data_size() is in items) chops a step into ~31 command\nbuffers committed while the CPU encodes the next; sanic encodes 263\ndispatches, commits once, waits. Moving MLX''s own caps prices it: 17.70 ms\nat ~124 cbufs, 16.38 at ~4 (their optimum), 17.11 at 1 — and with chopping\noff MLX runs 17.5 ms/tok, exactly sanic''s 17.5 in the same session.\n\nThe other candidate is closed by measurement: sanic emits 213 phases\nagainst a DAG floor of 180, but forcing a barrier before every dispatch\ncosts only ~0.15 ms/step, so the 33 recoverable phases are worth ≲0.1 ms.\nAt batch-1 decode the schedule''s value is when work is submitted, not what\nruns beside what.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"992b1efcb1f339a1ef5a26773ca5ae48edc5e8e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/992b1efcb1f339a1ef5a26773ca5ae48edc5e8e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/f2d2d664a685628c818d96a0d2f4f5ddfdf30fb2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/f2d2d664a685628c818d96a0d2f4f5ddfdf30fb2","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGYyZDJkNjY0YTY4NTYyOGM4MThkOTZhMGQyZjRmNWRkZmRmMzBmYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/8edd296d00a3c455ad9eb699810cb28f5ae842d5","sha":"8edd296d00a3c455ad9eb699810cb28f5ae842d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/8edd296d00a3c455ad9eb699810cb28f5ae842d5"}],"sha":"f2d2d664a685628c818d96a0d2f4f5ddfdf30fb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/f2d2d664a685628c818d96a0d2f4f5ddfdf30fb2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/8edd296d00a3c455ad9eb699810cb28f5ae842d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T05:19:53Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T05:19:53Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"wire the clock into the two things that judge timings — and llama never hits peak\n\ntune_fold_scheds now brackets every replay with a clock watch and\nDISCARDS samples the GPU ran below its top DVFS state, falling back to\nthe unfiltered minimum if it never reached peak. A throttled sample is\n~25% slow for reasons the schedule had nothing to do with, and would\nhand a candidate a win or a loss it did not earn. SANIC_DEBUG=2 prints\nthe clock on any step measured below peak, in yellow, rather than\npublishing a throttled number as if it were comparable.\n\nThe first run says something the whole day''s analysis assumed away:\n\n  20.20ms GPU  bw 61%   679 MHz, 26% busy\n  19.65ms GPU  bw 63%   892 MHz, 93% busy\n  18.13ms GPU  bw 68%   911 MHz, 92% busy\n  16.78ms GPU  bw 74%  1054 MHz, 91% busy\n\nPeak is 1296 MHz. llama decode NEVER reaches it — it sits around 900,\nand the fastest steps are simply the ones where the clock ran highest.\nSo every number measured today was taken at roughly 70% of the GPU''s\nclock, including the ones behind todo.md item 4''s \"kernels are at 97% of\npractical peak\" and \"184 GB/s is the ceiling\". Those were measured on a\nmachine that was not running flat out, and the 184 GB/s figure is\ntherefore a floor on the ceiling, not the ceiling.\n\nNot yet explained, and worth a session of its own: why the governor\nkeeps a 92%-busy GPU at 70% clock. A serial chain of short dependent\nkernels may simply not look like sustained load to it — in which case\nthe barrier cost measured earlier is understated, since serialization\nwould be depressing the clock as well as the overlap.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"71ddb891b9b111689c5bada6a6611736770a1e35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/71ddb891b9b111689c5bada6a6611736770a1e35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/8edd296d00a3c455ad9eb699810cb28f5ae842d5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/8edd296d00a3c455ad9eb699810cb28f5ae842d5","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDhlZGQyOTZkMDBhM2M0NTVhZDllYjY5OTgxMGNiMjhmNWFlODQyZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/f24bba3d5c4ce5557479a92f3e2c178b967e4d65","sha":"f24bba3d5c4ce5557479a92f3e2c178b967e4d65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/f24bba3d5c4ce5557479a92f3e2c178b967e4d65"}],"sha":"8edd296d00a3c455ad9eb699810cb28f5ae842d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/8edd296d00a3c455ad9eb699810cb28f5ae842d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/f24bba3d5c4ce5557479a92f3e2c178b967e4d65/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T05:16:08Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T05:16:08Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"device.clock(): measure the DVFS state a benchmark actually ran at\n\nApple GPUs do not run at one speed. They sit in discrete (frequency,\nvoltage) P-states — on this M1 Pro 0, 388.8, 486, 648, 777.6, 972,\n1296 MHz — and drop down when idle, warm, or sharing the package power\nbudget. A run that lands one state low is ~25% slower for reasons that\nhave nothing to do with the code, which is exactly the drift that forced\ntune_fold_scheds to re-measure a baseline beside every candidate rather\nthan compare against one taken at the start of a run.\n\nMetalDevice::clock() opens a ClockWatch; ClockWatch::read() closes the\nwindow and returns busy fraction, mean MHz while busy, and the device''s\npeak — with Clock::at_peak() as the question a caller actually asks: is\nthis measurement comparable to another one? It is a WINDOW, not an\ninstant, because IOReport residency is a delta between two samples, so\nthe API makes you bracket the work rather than pretend otherwise.\n\nUnprivileged and ~1 ms: group \"GPU Stats\", subgroup \"GPU Performance\nStates\", channel GPUPH, ticks of a 24 MHz counter; the state index to\nMHz table comes from the device tree (IODeviceTree:/arm-io/pmgr,\nproperty voltage-states9) rather than from the accelerator. Device-wide\nrather than per-process, which is documented rather than hidden — it is\nalso how \"something else was using the GPU during my benchmark\" becomes\nvisible.\n\nThe new test earns its keep immediately: a short spin workload reports\n938 MHz against a 1296 MHz peak, at_peak false. That window was 28% slow\nbefore any code was involved.\n\nNot pinnable, only measurable — Instruments'' own minimum/medium/maximum\nsettings all leave this GPU at its top state — so the honest response to\nat_peak() == false is to discard the sample, which is what the doc says.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e1f4225cc896bf32cb64978e6e68ecfc85b62bac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/e1f4225cc896bf32cb64978e6e68ecfc85b62bac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/f24bba3d5c4ce5557479a92f3e2c178b967e4d65","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/f24bba3d5c4ce5557479a92f3e2c178b967e4d65","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGYyNGJiYTNkNWM0Y2U1NTU3NDc5YTkyZjNlMmMxNzhiOTY3ZTRkNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/798aee1d802c5dc10c30d39ee95a4cd4ab4e40f8","sha":"798aee1d802c5dc10c30d39ee95a4cd4ab4e40f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/798aee1d802c5dc10c30d39ee95a4cd4ab4e40f8"}],"sha":"f24bba3d5c4ce5557479a92f3e2c178b967e4d65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/f24bba3d5c4ce5557479a92f3e2c178b967e4d65"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/798aee1d802c5dc10c30d39ee95a4cd4ab4e40f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T01:47:57Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T01:47:57Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"the GPU counters ARE reachable — out of process, and the wall is an entitlement\n\nCorrecting the previous commit, which concluded from the documented\nsurface that the rich counters were unreachable. Undocumented is not\nabsent: they are absent from OUR PROCESS, not from the machine.\n\nIN-PROCESS: closed, and now known exactly where. The private API is all\npresent on the real classes (AGXG13XDevice -> IOGPUMetalDevice ->\n_MTLDevice): supportsGPUStatistics returns 1, and there are\nrequestCounters:, addPerfSampleHandler:, runPerfCounterCallbackWithBlock:,\nnewSample, resolveCounters:withRange:. All return nil/0 unentitled.\nDisassembling AGXGPURawCounterImpl::init and reproducing it standalone\nfinds the wall precisely: IOConnectCallStructMethod(gpu, selector 261)\n-> kIOReturnNotPrivileged, while neighbouring selectors 0x100-0x104 are\nungated. NOT SIP — SIP is disabled on this machine and it still refuses;\nit is AMFI enforcing com.apple.private.gputools.client, which\ngputoolsserviced carries and a self-signed binary cannot.\n\nOUT-OF-PROCESS: open, verified working. Instruments injects nothing into\nthe target — diffing _dyld_image_count and the full class list under\nfour templates gives byte-identical results — so there was never a call\nsequence to trace; collection runs in the entitled daemon. Driving\nusage: xctrace record [<options>] [--attach | --all-processes | --launch -- command ]\n\ndescription:\n\tPerform a new recording on the specified device and target with the given template\n\noptions:\n\t--output <path>                        Output .trace file to the given path\n\t--append-run                           Appends a new run to an existing trace file\n\t--run-name <name>                      Names the run\n\t--template <path|name>                 Record using given trace template name or path\n\t--device <name|UDID>                   Record on device with the given name or UDID\n\t--instrument <name>                    Add Instrument with the given name to the recording\n\t--time-limit <time[ms|s|m|h]>          Limit recording time to the specified value\n\t--window <duration[ms|s|m]>            Keep only events from the specified end time window\n\t--package <file>                       Load Instruments Package from given path for duration of the command\n\t--all-processes                        Record all processes\n\t--attach <pid|name>                    Attach and record process with the given name or pid\n\t--launch -- command [arguments]        Launch process with the given name or path\n\t--target-stdin <name>                  Redirect standard input of the launched process\n\t--target-stdout <name>                 Redirect standard output of the launched process\n\t--env <VAR=value>                      Set specified environment variable for the launched process\n\t--notify-tracing-started               Send Darwin notification with this name when a recording has started\n\t--no-prompt                            Skip any prompts that would be otherwise presented (like privacy warnings)\n\nglobal options:\n\t--quiet        Make terminal ouput less verbose\n\nnotes:\n\tIf an output path is not specified, a uniquely named file will be created in the current directory.\n\tIf the output path is a directory, then a unique file is created in it. If the path contains the .trace\n\textension, a file will be created at the specified path. If trace file already exists, then --append-run\n\tneeds to be specified to add a run to it. In this case, specified template will be ignored\n\tand the one used to record original trace file will be used.\n\n\tIf target device UDID or name is not specified — host device is used for the recording.\n\tSpecifying environment variables or stream redirection is only available when using launch option.\n\nexamples:\n\txctrace record --template ''Time Profiler'' --all-processes --time-limit 5s\n\txctrace record --template ''Time Profiler'' --all-processes --output ''recording.trace''\n\txctrace record --all-processes --append-run --run-name Fix#2 --output ''existing.trace''\n\txctrace record --template ''System Trace'' --attach 4215\n\txctrace record --template ''Time Profiler'' --device-name \"Chad''s iPhone\" --attach ''Trailblazer''\n\txctrace record --template ''Metal System Trace'' --device-name ''iPhone SE Simulator'' --all-processes\n\txctrace record --template ''Allocations'' --env KEY=VALUE --launch -- MyApp.app\n\txctrace record --template ''Time Profiler'' --target-stdout - --launch -- /tmp/tool arg1 arg2 needs no root and no\nDeveloper Mode and yields all 31 counters at 20us: ALU Limiter, Buffer\nRead/Write Limiter, GPU Last Level Cache Limiter, Compute Occupancy, GPU\nRead/Write Bandwidth. Validated against a two-phase FMA/stream workload\n(ALU 94% then Buffer Write 72%). Counters are GPU-wide, so quiesce the\nmachine.\n\nIOReport: open, unprivileged, ~1 ms, and the piece worth wiring in.\nGroup \"GPU Stats\" / \"GPU Performance States\" / channel GPUPH gives DVFS\nresidency; the index->MHz table is the device tree''s pmgr\nvoltage-states9. Verified idle at 55% OFF / 45% P1 and a Metal load\npinned at 100% P6 / 1296 MHz. This is the sanity gate every benchmark in\ntodo.md should have had — the clock drift that forced the tuner''s\nper-family adjacent baselines is directly measurable now.\n\nAlso recorded: the GPU performance state can be REQUESTED but does not\nmove the clock here (Min/Med/Max all measured ~P6), and\nAGXMetalStatisticsExternalA14X-counters.plist holds 276 derived counters\nfor this exact GPU including the absolute Bytes Read From Main Memory\nthat xctrace will not give us.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"79a102dc2b8cfa844e4adfda7dff64d09f1ccfaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/79a102dc2b8cfa844e4adfda7dff64d09f1ccfaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/798aee1d802c5dc10c30d39ee95a4cd4ab4e40f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/798aee1d802c5dc10c30d39ee95a4cd4ab4e40f8","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDc5OGFlZTFkODAyYzVkYzEwYzMwZDM5ZWU5NWE0Y2Q0YWI0ZTQwZjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/5cf71fc30aa479ee4d4864f36795d57ecc837c52","sha":"5cf71fc30aa479ee4d4864f36795d57ecc837c52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/5cf71fc30aa479ee4d4864f36795d57ecc837c52"}],"sha":"798aee1d802c5dc10c30d39ee95a4cd4ab4e40f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/798aee1d802c5dc10c30d39ee95a4cd4ab4e40f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/5cf71fc30aa479ee4d4864f36795d57ecc837c52/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T01:09:47Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T01:09:47Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"SANIC_GPUTRACE: the counters worth having are not in the API, so emit a capture\n\nRead Apple''s material on GPU counters (WWDC20 \"Optimize Metal apps and\ngames with GPU counters\"). The thing worth having is the performance\nLIMITER — ALU, buffer read/write, last-level cache, tile memory — which\nsays WHY a kernel is slow where a timestamp only says how slow. 150+\ncounters exist, including bytes read from main memory and occupancy.\n\nThen asked this machine what it will hand to code:\n\n  sampling points: AtStageBoundary only\n  counter sets:    timestamp, containing one counter, GPUTimestamp\n\nThat is all. No stage-utilization, no statistics, no memory or occupancy\ncounters — and not gated by environment either (tried\nMETAL_CAPTURE_ENABLED, MTL_CAPTURE_ENABLED, METAL_DEVICE_WRAPPER_TYPE,\nMTL_COUNTERS_ENABLED; the set is one, always). So run_kernel_timed was\nalready spending the entire programmatic budget and there is no richer\ncounter to add.\n\nSANIC_GPUTRACE=<path> is the way through: with METAL_CAPTURE_ENABLED=1\nit captures one graph replay into a .gputrace document that opens in\nXcode with all 150+ counters, per dispatch — each dispatch already\ncarrying the descriptive kernel name this compiler generates, each\ncommand buffer its step label. Verified end to end on llama (2.3 GB\ntrace, tokens unchanged). That is how to check by measurement what\ntodo.md item 4 currently claims by inference: real DRAM bytes against\nour logical estimate, real occupancy, and which limiter each fold sits\non.\n\nRecorded alongside it, unexplored: those counters reach Instruments\nsomehow, so they are reachable — through the AGX accelerator''s IOKit\nuser client, reversed the way tinygrad''s ops_nv/ops_amd bypass\nCUDA/ROCm. Cheaper first rungs: IOReport channels for GPU busy% and\nFREQUENCY, which would explain the clock drift that confounded every\nmeasurement today and forced the tuner''s per-family adjacent baselines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"04610dc6f2e71f6cefd68cd7150ceebb93b6562a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/04610dc6f2e71f6cefd68cd7150ceebb93b6562a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/5cf71fc30aa479ee4d4864f36795d57ecc837c52","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/5cf71fc30aa479ee4d4864f36795d57ecc837c52","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDVjZjcxZmMzMGFhNDc5ZWU0ZDQ4NjRmMzY3OTVkNTdlY2M4MzdjNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/78f270ac6785cefeb6d8d9ee3271f70aa7e240b8","sha":"78f270ac6785cefeb6d8d9ee3271f70aa7e240b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/78f270ac6785cefeb6d8d9ee3271f70aa7e240b8"}],"sha":"5cf71fc30aa479ee4d4864f36795d57ecc837c52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/5cf71fc30aa479ee4d4864f36795d57ecc837c52"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/78f270ac6785cefeb6d8d9ee3271f70aa7e240b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T00:31:52Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T00:31:52Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"what MLX does, measured: the same shape, the same floor, the same reason\n\nMLX''s rms_norm.metal IS the two-pass row-resident kernel — accumulate\nthe sum of squares, threadgroup-reduce, second pass writes the row; one\nkernel where sanic emits two. So the shape was right and the earlier\nattempt was a bad implementation of a good idea. Timed head to head:\n\n  reduce+apply 8.00us   fused, MLX''s shape 7.71us   1.04x\n\n0.29 us per norm. 9 us per step. 0.06%. The whole normalizer fusion is\nworth nothing measurable, which retires the ~0.8 ms estimate for good.\n\nIt also corrects my own \"7.9 us per barrier\", which was (15.55-13.87)/212\n— an average that assumed the entire gap was barrier overhead. A barrier\nbetween two dependent kernels costs ~0.3 us. What barriers=none actually\nbuys is letting the seven big DRAM-bound matmuls of a layer run\nCONCURRENTLY, filling each other''s ramp. The 1.68 ms is the cost of a\nserial dependency chain, not of synchronization — which is precisely\nwhat all three closed fusion directions kept failing to find.\n\nA persistent megakernel would not recover it either: keeping\nthreadgroups resident removes drain-and-refill, but layer N+1''s matmul\nstill cannot begin before layer N''s output exists. The serialization is\nin the model, not the runtime.\n\nSo ~15.5 ms is the floor for batch-1 decode of this model on this\nmachine with this decomposition, and MLX sits at the same floor for the\nsame reason — same chain, same seven GEMVs, its kernels at the same\n184 GB/s ceiling. The parity measured earlier today is not a\ncoincidence; both are bandwidth-bound on identical traffic with\nidentical dependencies. Going faster means breaking the serialization —\nspeculative decoding, batching, quantization — not sharpening kernels.\ntodo.md item 4 now says so and closes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2822a0cfe98a5c4bad39835d7dc8f2ba62bd8fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/b2822a0cfe98a5c4bad39835d7dc8f2ba62bd8fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/78f270ac6785cefeb6d8d9ee3271f70aa7e240b8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/78f270ac6785cefeb6d8d9ee3271f70aa7e240b8","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDc4ZjI3MGFjNjc4NWNlZmViNmQ4ZDllZTMyNzFmNzBhYTdlMjQwYjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/a0234b30e55e68ad2827bc37100cc342ef00707a","sha":"a0234b30e55e68ad2827bc37100cc342ef00707a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/a0234b30e55e68ad2827bc37100cc342ef00707a"}],"sha":"78f270ac6785cefeb6d8d9ee3271f70aa7e240b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/78f270ac6785cefeb6d8d9ee3271f70aa7e240b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/a0234b30e55e68ad2827bc37100cc342ef00707a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T00:18:27Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T00:18:27Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"sideways fusion is closed too, and the barrier count already proved it\n\nMerging independent equally-parallel kernels — q|k|v into one dispatch,\ngate|up into one — keeps every thread, so neither law from the previous\ntwo attempts touches it. It still saves nothing, and no probe was needed\nto find that out: 263 dispatches with 212 barriers means 51 dispatches\nride an earlier barrier for free, and the layer structure predicts\nexactly 3 per layer x 16 = 48 (k and v riding q''s barrier, up riding\ngate''s) plus the prologue. Exact match. Those kernels are ALREADY\nconcurrent within their phase; merging them removes zero barriers and\nonly ~0.1 ms of CPU encode, which the GPU hides.\n\nThat closes all three fusion directions:\n  consumer rides producer   -> inherits a 1-threadgroup geometry\n  producer into consumer    -> trades away threads (the block-rows law)\n  independent kernels merged-> already concurrent\n\nThe 212 barriers are true data dependencies of a serial transformer at\nbatch 1, ~7.9 us of pipeline drain each, and fusion cannot remove them.\n\nWhat remains is not a fusion but a different execution model: keep\nthreadgroups resident across phases and synchronize inside the kernel\nrather than at kernel boundaries — the persistent/megakernel shape. It\nwants its own probe before any machinery: two dependent GEMVs as one\npersistent kernel against two dispatches, to find out whether a\ndevice-scope barrier actually costs less than 7.9 us on Apple silicon.\nIf it does not, 15.5 ms is the floor for this decomposition and the\nhonest thing is to say so. todo.md item 4 records it that way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b73e2317cce8e39e58abfd9844c1c59739dc6a97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/b73e2317cce8e39e58abfd9844c1c59739dc6a97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/a0234b30e55e68ad2827bc37100cc342ef00707a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/a0234b30e55e68ad2827bc37100cc342ef00707a","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGEwMjM0YjMwZTU1ZTY4YWQyODI3YmMzNzEwMGNjMzQyZWYwMDcwN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/c7024e81a5187c916081e8c3629eb8b19b0ff8d6","sha":"c7024e81a5187c916081e8c3629eb8b19b0ff8d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/c7024e81a5187c916081e8c3629eb8b19b0ff8d6"}],"sha":"a0234b30e55e68ad2827bc37100cc342ef00707a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/a0234b30e55e68ad2827bc37100cc342ef00707a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/c7024e81a5187c916081e8c3629eb8b19b0ff8d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T00:02:48Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T00:02:48Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"measure the block-rows theory before building it: it loses 1.6x\n\nThe reasoned \"perfect\" shape for a batch-1 projection was: give each\nthreadgroup a BLOCK of output rows, stage the activation row in\nthreadgroup memory, and fold the normalizer once during that staging —\nso RMSNorm fuses into its consumer with the reduction amortized over the\nblock instead of recomputed per output point.\n\ntests/block_rows_probe.rs writes both shapes by hand, checks they agree,\nand times them:\n\n  three kernels 132us   block-rows fused 218us   0.61x\n\nBlocking rows is the one thing batch-1 decode cannot afford: it trades\naway THREADS. Per-point runs 2048 threadgroups — 524k threads, 8\nelements each. Block-rows runs 256 — 65k threads, 64 each. Sustained\nbandwidth is outstanding bytes over latency, so 8x fewer threads is 8x\nfewer loads in flight, and 8 KB of staged activation caps residency per\ncore besides. The projection is DRAM-bound; parallelism is the whole\ngame and amortized arithmetic buys nothing.\n\nThe law this establishes, and the reason the test is kept as a pinned\nregression guard rather than deleted: ON THIS MACHINE A FUSION THAT\nREDUCES THREAD COUNT IS A REGRESSION, EVEN WHEN IT REMOVES A KERNEL AND\nA BARRIER. That kills block-rows and P2 rows-per-thread — for a second\nand better reason than \"the kernels are already at peak\" — and it\nexplains the previous attempt too: making the apply ride the reduce\ninherited a one-threadgroup geometry.\n\nBoth known ways to absorb the starved kernels are now closed. What is\nuntried is fusing SIDEWAYS — q|k|v into one dispatch, gate|up into one,\nthe rope halves, the cache writes: independent, equally parallel work\nthat keeps every thread and still deletes a phase each. todo.md item 4\nrecords that as the next thing to measure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6d24e540e70520cd92b4e7bbb04c355143b54edf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/6d24e540e70520cd92b4e7bbb04c355143b54edf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/c7024e81a5187c916081e8c3629eb8b19b0ff8d6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/c7024e81a5187c916081e8c3629eb8b19b0ff8d6","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGM3MDI0ZTgxYTUxODdjOTE2MDgxZThjMzYyOWViOGIxOWIwZmY4ZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/926c3847e59b72fbc4bc59544e2e1014822ad321","sha":"926c3847e59b72fbc4bc59544e2e1014822ad321","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/926c3847e59b72fbc4bc59544e2e1014822ad321"}],"sha":"c7024e81a5187c916081e8c3629eb8b19b0ff8d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/c7024e81a5187c916081e8c3629eb8b19b0ff8d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/926c3847e59b72fbc4bc59544e2e1014822ad321/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T22:30:38Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T22:30:38Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"record why the first two-pass attempt lost: it inherits the fold''s geometry\n\nBuilt the two-pass row-resident kernel and reverted it. It worked\nstructurally — epilogue_rides relaxed to admit a host the cone\nbroadcasts over one reduced axis, both Metal emitters given a pass two\n(project into threadgroup memory, barrier, stripe the row) — and it\nfused exactly as designed: 263→230 dispatches, 212→179 barriers, llama\ntext unchanged.\n\nIt was still slower: 17.4 vs 15.0 ms/tok.\n\nThe reason is geometric, and it is the thing to fix before trying\nagain: a fused kernel inherits the FOLD''s launch geometry. The RMS\nreduce dispatches one threadgroup (its output is a single point), so\npass two writes 2048 elements with 256 threads where the separate map\nkernel had 2048 threads over two threadgroups. The fusion buys one\nbarrier and pays 8x the parallelism of the apply. It also NaN''d\nattention_backward_runs_on_gpu (dq), so the coordinate mapping is not\nright for gradient folds either.\n\nA next attempt has to size the two-pass kernel''s threadgroups by the\nROW it writes, not by the fold''s output — a split two-stage reduction,\nor a schedule whose sgs is large enough that one threadgroup covers the\nrow. Until then the separate map kernel is the better shape, and item\n4''s ~0.8 ms estimate is an upper bound the geometry does not allow\ncollecting. Recorded in todo.md item 4 so the next attempt starts from\nthe measurement rather than the idea.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d45d4709ce746ca441752b9e46de3b8bb46ef6f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/d45d4709ce746ca441752b9e46de3b8bb46ef6f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/926c3847e59b72fbc4bc59544e2e1014822ad321","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/926c3847e59b72fbc4bc59544e2e1014822ad321","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDkyNmMzODQ3ZTU5YjcyZmJjNGJjNTk1NDRlMmUxMDE0ODIyYWQzMjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/da181eb8687a1b984d97047e00e99d5c383c31b3","sha":"da181eb8687a1b984d97047e00e99d5c383c31b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/da181eb8687a1b984d97047e00e99d5c383c31b3"}],"sha":"926c3847e59b72fbc4bc59544e2e1014822ad321","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/926c3847e59b72fbc4bc59544e2e1014822ad321"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/da181eb8687a1b984d97047e00e99d5c383c31b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T22:20:34Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T22:20:34Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"the remaining gap is synchronization, and the barrier count says so\n\nSANIC_DEBUG=3 now prints a captured graph''s dispatch and barrier count:\nllama decode is 263 dispatches in 213 serial phases.\n\nThat number, plus a barriers=none floor run (deliberately racy, used\nonly as a floor), decomposes the 15.55 ms bf16 step:\n\n  traffic floor at 184 GB/s   13.48 ms   (2480 MB, irreducible: every\n                                          weight read once, 0.8% over)\n  measured, barriers=none     13.87 ms   97% of practical peak\n  measured, real barriers     15.55 ms\n  = synchronization            1.68 ms   11%, 212 barriers x 7.9 us\n\nSo the generated kernels are essentially optimal — 184 GB/s is the\nceiling MLX''s best kernel reaches too — and the whole remaining gap is\nphase count. This retires P2/rows-per-thread and further wide-load work\nas dead ends, and makes FUSION the only lever.\n\n134 of 263 dispatches are starved (<=8 of 16 cores) while being 8.8% of\nkernel time. The biggest single item is the normalizer: 32 RMS reduces\nat ONE threadgroup plus 32 applies at two, ~0.8 ms with their barriers.\ntodo.md item 4 records the decomposition, the starved families and the\nfusion each wants, and what precisely blocks the two-pass row-resident\nkernel: emit_cone requires an epilogue host of exactly the cone''s shape,\nbut the RMS denominator is [1,1] against a [1,2048] cone. interp and\nrustgen already handle a broadcast epilogue; only the Metal emitter\nneeds the second pass.\n\nAlso recorded because it cost an experiment: deferring the divisor\ninstead (SANIC_DIVCUT=never) is 10x SLOWER — 170 ms — because the\nnormalizer is then recomputed per output point. The cost model is right\nto cut; the missing option is computing it once per threadgroup.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dc99309c11c6bd7498b6f17f095ccd075baa4cec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/dc99309c11c6bd7498b6f17f095ccd075baa4cec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/da181eb8687a1b984d97047e00e99d5c383c31b3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/da181eb8687a1b984d97047e00e99d5c383c31b3","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGRhMTgxZWI4Njg3YTFiOTg0ZDk3MDQ3ZTAwZTk5ZDVjMzgzYzMxYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/d99bdcacac6acf155968f33b3d75032366532dfa","sha":"d99bdcacac6acf155968f33b3d75032366532dfa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/d99bdcacac6acf155968f33b3d75032366532dfa"}],"sha":"da181eb8687a1b984d97047e00e99d5c383c31b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/da181eb8687a1b984d97047e00e99d5c383c31b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/d99bdcacac6acf155968f33b3d75032366532dfa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T21:47:00Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T21:47:00Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"count decode STEPS, not tokens, in the MLX comparison\n\nThe first token falls out of the prefill logits and costs no decode step,\nso examples/llama3_2.rs runs 63 steps for -n 64 — and its printed\n\"decode tok/s\" is already steps/s while \"generated\" is tokens. Dividing\nthe printed elapsed by tokens compared sanic''s 63 steps against MLX''s 64\nand flattered sanic by ~1.5%.\n\nCorrected, per decode step: sanic tuned 16.2 ms (61.6/s), mlx-lm 16.2 ms\n(61.8/s) — still parity, with MLX a hair ahead rather than behind.\n\nThe row that matters is unchanged and now stated plainly: sanic''s GPU step\nis 15.3 ms, already below MLX''s total wall. The ~0.9 ms/step it gives back\nis host work — re-encoding 263 dispatches, and reading all 128k logits to\nthe CPU to argmax them there, which MLX does on the GPU.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8cc118a6c5fcfcc42c11bd9e1b744109e51cb2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/c8cc118a6c5fcfcc42c11bd9e1b744109e51cb2e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/d99bdcacac6acf155968f33b3d75032366532dfa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/d99bdcacac6acf155968f33b3d75032366532dfa","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGQ5OWJkY2FjYWM2YWNmMTU1OTY4ZjMzYjNkNzUwMzIzNjY1MzJkZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/a72d3f62583e0cee597c6245ec6599da0dc78335","sha":"a72d3f62583e0cee597c6245ec6599da0dc78335","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/a72d3f62583e0cee597c6245ec6599da0dc78335"}],"sha":"d99bdcacac6acf155968f33b3d75032366532dfa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/d99bdcacac6acf155968f33b3d75032366532dfa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/a72d3f62583e0cee597c6245ec6599da0dc78335/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T21:43:00Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T21:43:00Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"parity with MLX on llama-3.2-1B, measured head to head\n\nSame M1 Pro, same model size and dtype, batch-1 greedy decode, prefill\nexcluded, 64 tokens, three trials each. MLX 0.32.0 / mlx-lm 0.31.3 on\nmlx-community/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct-bf16; sanic on meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B\nthrough the public library API.\n\n  sanic tuned   15.9 ms/tok wall (61.6 tok/s), 15.3 ms GPU\n  mlx-lm bf16   16.2 ms/tok wall (61.8 tok/s)\n\nParity, within the ~1% these trials resolve — against the framework whose\nkernels are hand-written for this hardware, with kernels sanic derived\nfrom naive dataflow by algebra. The three rungs that closed it all landed\ntoday: in-graph per-kernel timestamps (which found that 15% of every step\nwas inter-encoder bubbles), one concurrent encoder per graph with barriers\nderived at capture, and the measured tuner.\n\nRecorded at the top of vs_mlx.md with the honest edges — MLX grows its KV\ncache while sanic bakes a fixed extent into the graph, and sanic''s wall\nstill carries ~0.6 ms/tok of CPU encode above its GPU time. The MLX side\nof the benchmark is weights/mlx_llama_bench.py so the number reproduces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5d7ad7ed4b0270568855669c2d84b689a7d3054b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/5d7ad7ed4b0270568855669c2d84b689a7d3054b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/a72d3f62583e0cee597c6245ec6599da0dc78335","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/a72d3f62583e0cee597c6245ec6599da0dc78335","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGE3MmQzZjYyNTgzZTBjZWU1OTdjNjI0NWVjNjU5OWRhMGRjNzgzMzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/725a1e5bbf83c48417ff87c42832ff679c3d70ef","sha":"725a1e5bbf83c48417ff87c42832ff679c3d70ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/725a1e5bbf83c48417ff87c42832ff679c3d70ef"}],"sha":"a72d3f62583e0cee597c6245ec6599da0dc78335","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/a72d3f62583e0cee597c6245ec6599da0dc78335"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/725a1e5bbf83c48417ff87c42832ff679c3d70ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T21:30:35Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T21:30:35Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"SANIC_TUNE: the device overrules the cost model, measured in context\n\nThe candidate enumeration has advertised a measured tuner since it was\nwritten; the counter-sample timer and the concurrent encoder finally\nmade one honest. `priced_fold_sched_candidates` is now the single rule\nwith two readers — the analytic chooser ranks by the price, the tuner\ntimes the feasible entries on the real machine — and\n`emit_schedule_metal_tuned` takes the verdicts, keyed by the fused\nstage''s output name.\n\nMeasured, llama-3.2-1B decode on M1 Pro: bf16 15.8→14.9 ms/step\n(60.2→63.5 tok/s), f32 18.7→16.1 ms (51.2→59.4 tok/s). It costs compile\ntime (5.2→13.3s), so it is opt-in.\n\nTwo designs were wrong before this one, and both lessons are in the\ncode:\n\n- SOLO TIMING IS A LIAR. Timing each candidate as its own dispatch —\n  the obvious design, and exactly what run_kernel_timed invites — chose\n  winners that made the real step ~12% SLOWER. A candidate re-reading\n  warm scratch is rewarded for parallelism that a DRAM-bound step\n  punishes. So the instrument is the step itself: substitute the\n  candidate into the full dispatch list over zeroed bindings, capture,\n  and replay. Isomorphic stages swap together as one family (keyed on\n  the scalar probe''s canonical source) and one wall time judges them.\n\n- EVERY VERDICT IS A DIFFERENCE OF ADJACENT MEASUREMENTS. The GPU clock\n  drifts across a tuning run: against a start-of-run baseline every\n  family \"won\" ~0.5ms, and the combined program then shipped none of\n  it. Each family now re-measures its own baseline beside its rivals,\n  overruling needs a 1% margin, and the whole tuned program must beat a\n  fresh baseline or nothing ships at all.\n\nAlso: the price triple became `SchedPrice { time, flops, additive }`\n(three bare f64s in a tuple said nothing), families under 2% of planned\ntime are skipped, and the env switches are listed together in lib.rs.\n\nGated by running the oracle suites with SANIC_TUNE=1 — tuned kernels\nare checked against the interpreter, not just timed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6f9dc43e1e781f1b2db7827ebdc96172e28709e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/6f9dc43e1e781f1b2db7827ebdc96172e28709e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/725a1e5bbf83c48417ff87c42832ff679c3d70ef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/725a1e5bbf83c48417ff87c42832ff679c3d70ef","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDcyNWExZTViYmY4M2M0ODQxN2ZmODdjNDI4MzJmZjY3OWMzZDcwZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/638e9d44047cb630a0541a4113001893faebaa4d","sha":"638e9d44047cb630a0541a4113001893faebaa4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/638e9d44047cb630a0541a4113001893faebaa4d"}],"sha":"725a1e5bbf83c48417ff87c42832ff679c3d70ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/725a1e5bbf83c48417ff87c42832ff679c3d70ef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/638e9d44047cb630a0541a4113001893faebaa4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T20:50:25Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T20:50:25Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"SANIC_MSL dumps the generated source; the profile after overlap, read\n\nSANIC_MSL=<path> writes the whole emitted MSL at prepare — the raw\nartifact behind every kernel name the runtime dumps print. First use\nanswered why 16 \"isomorphic\" layers emit 33 distinct norm folds: the\nresidual stream is never materialized, so layer N''s RMSNorm fold\nre-sums all N+2 prior residual contributions in-register — growing\narity, genuinely non-isomorphic, dedup was right all along. Correct\nat batch-1 decode (re-reading k×4KB beats a materialize round-trip);\nrevisit at long-context prefill where the re-reads grow with depth.\n\ntodo.md item 2 re-measured in the concurrent-encoder regime: the tiny\nnorm folds are down to ~700µs profiled (less in production, hidden by\noverlap) — the two-pass fusion feature is parked. The post-overlap\nprofile says the remaining MLX gap is fold DRAM rate: MLP down-proj\n77% bw, up+gate 85%, logits 90% — P1 chunk+wide-loads and the\nmeasured tuner are the attack.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7bad4ae36a49acbeb4229adffefa0ec7b53c1d77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/7bad4ae36a49acbeb4229adffefa0ec7b53c1d77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/638e9d44047cb630a0541a4113001893faebaa4d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/638e9d44047cb630a0541a4113001893faebaa4d","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDYzOGU5ZDQ0MDQ3Y2I2MzBhMDU0MWE0MTEzMDAxODkzZmFlYmFhNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/6bd7bed49b27e0d2c6597aa735ac2290b8694fed","sha":"6bd7bed49b27e0d2c6597aa735ac2290b8694fed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/6bd7bed49b27e0d2c6597aa735ac2290b8694fed"}],"sha":"638e9d44047cb630a0541a4113001893faebaa4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/638e9d44047cb630a0541a4113001893faebaa4d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/6bd7bed49b27e0d2c6597aa735ac2290b8694fed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T20:45:20Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T20:45:20Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"one concurrent encoder per graph: barriers derived at capture, ICB retired\n\nThe in-graph timer forced this: a 263-kernel llama step was 263 compute\nencoders in one command buffer, and each encoder boundary idled the GPU\n~10-16µs — 22.3ms wall against 19.4ms Σ kernels, ~15% of every step\nspent between kernels. Metal only hazard-tracks BETWEEN encoders, so\nper-kernel encoders were how ordering stayed correct.\n\nThe replacement is one execution law for every dispatch list, run and\nreplay alike (encode_graph + barrier_schedule): a single\nMTLDispatchTypeConcurrent encoder, dispatches back-to-back, and a\nbuffer-scope memoryBarrier exactly where the capture-time analysis finds\na dependency frontier. Sanic knows the whole graph statically — unlike\nMLX, which tracks the same hazards dynamically per step (its\nCommandEncoder wrapper: prev/next buffer sets + maybeInsertBarrier) —\nso the barrier schedule is derived once at capture. Conflicts are\nRAW/WAR/WAW per underlying allocation, deliberately conservative on\nslices (the zero-copy weights file is one allocation, read-only). A\nbarrier is a phase boundary — everything after waits on everything\nbefore — so the walk resets both access histories at each one; a second\nconsumer of a producer rides the first consumer''s barrier for free\n(barrier_before''s unit test pins these semantics). Inside a concurrent\nencoder Metal does NO hazard tracking, so the schedule is load-bearing:\nrun() takes the same path precisely so the whole oracle suite gates it.\n\nMeasured (M1 Pro, llama-3.2-1B decode): f32 22.3→18.9ms/step\n(40.9→49.6 tok/s); bf16 23.5→15.6ms (59.7 tok/s) at bw 79%. plan Σ\nsnapped from ×1.25 to ×1.04 — the encoder bubbles WERE most of the\ncost-model miscalibration. The wall now sits BELOW the old Σ kernels:\nindependent stages genuinely overlap.\n\nREMOVED, and why — recover everything from this commit''s parent if ICB\nis ever explored again (git show <this>^:src/metal.rs):\n- MetalGraphExecution::{Direct,Indirect}, MetalIndirectCommandBuffer,\n  capture_indirect, the executeCommandsInBuffer raw msg_send,\n  icb_resource_usages, icb_command_needs_barrier (ICB-semantics\n  hazard analysis: a barrier belongs to one command, histories never\n  reset — the inverse of the phase-boundary walk that replaced it).\n- MAX_INDIRECT_COMMANDS = 64, the u32-offset panic (ICB offsets are\n  u32 on the wire; zero-copy weight slices exceed it), the residency\n  set making buffers AND pipelines resident, and every pipeline''s\n  setSupportIndirectCommandBuffers opt-in.\n\nICB felt like the correct solution — encode once, replay with one\nexecuteCommandsInBuffer, near-zero CPU re-encode; it is what tinygrad\nships. It lost on evidence, not taste: >64-command concurrent ICBs\nfault on Apple7 EVEN AFTER the pipeline-residency fix (fb1b54f fixed\ntinygrad''s FIX_METAL_ICB crash properly; 4d200c1 then still had to cap\nat 64 — the instability postdates the fix and has no known cause). The\nconcurrent encoder expresses the same coarse barrier schedule with no\nwire format, no cap, no quirk, and its CPU re-encode costs a few\nhundred µs against a 19ms step. Revisit ICB only on Apple9+ hardware\n(both quirks gone, per tinygrad''s needs_icb_fix gate) and only if\nper-step CPU encode measurably matters. The full story:\nvs_tinygrad.md § \"The Metal ICB residency lesson\", todo.md item 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"67642a4960c03cd8cda1d9725c8ea485aa0379f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/67642a4960c03cd8cda1d9725c8ea485aa0379f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/6bd7bed49b27e0d2c6597aa735ac2290b8694fed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/6bd7bed49b27e0d2c6597aa735ac2290b8694fed","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDZiZDdiZWQ0OWIyN2UwZDJjNjU5N2FhNzM1YWMyMjkwYjg2OTRmZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/7bfa9d41e13c9a01d49629d97a82c5ad1c3331c4","sha":"7bfa9d41e13c9a01d49629d97a82c5ad1c3331c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/7bfa9d41e13c9a01d49629d97a82c5ad1c3331c4"}],"sha":"6bd7bed49b27e0d2c6597aa735ac2290b8694fed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/6bd7bed49b27e0d2c6597aa735ac2290b8694fed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/7bfa9d41e13c9a01d49629d97a82c5ad1c3331c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T20:26:04Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T20:26:04Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"write down the timing arc''s next steps and the ICB lesson\n\ntodo.md gains \"Runtime timing arc\": the four items the in-graph\ntimer says to do, with the decided design for the biggest one — one\nconcurrent encoder per frozen graph, direct dispatches, barriers\ncomputed at capture time from the existing conflict analysis; both\ncurrent replay paths (encoder-per-dispatch and the 64-capped ICB)\nfold into that one law.\n\nvs_tinygrad.md gains \"The Metal ICB residency lesson\", so it is not\nre-learned: MTLBuffer and MTLComputePipelineState both conform to\nMTLAllocation, so one residency set makes buffers AND pipelines\nresident (fb1b54f) — the first-class fix for the fault tinygrad''s\nFIX_METAL_ICB dummy-dispatches around. Separately, >64-command\nconcurrent ICBs stayed unstable on Apple7 AFTER that fix (4d200c1):\ntwo distinct failure modes, only the first has a clean fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e336ead9fde1d037b4cb71fab0ba65b0d2ee43f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/e336ead9fde1d037b4cb71fab0ba65b0d2ee43f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/7bfa9d41e13c9a01d49629d97a82c5ad1c3331c4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/7bfa9d41e13c9a01d49629d97a82c5ad1c3331c4","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDdiZmE5ZDQxZTEzYzlhMDFkNDk2MjlkOTdhODJjNWFkMWMzMzMxYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/90451e65d6bd6d11852b792f957c0e51fc8885f5","sha":"90451e65d6bd6d11852b792f957c0e51fc8885f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/90451e65d6bd6d11852b792f957c0e51fc8885f5"}],"sha":"7bfa9d41e13c9a01d49629d97a82c5ad1c3331c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/7bfa9d41e13c9a01d49629d97a82c5ad1c3331c4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/90451e65d6bd6d11852b792f957c0e51fc8885f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T20:26:04Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T20:26:04Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"the runtime dump measures inside the graph and names what it sees\n\n- SANIC_DEBUG=4 times every kernel INSIDE the replayed command buffer:\n  a timestamp counter sample buffer brackets each encoder (stage\n  boundaries are the only sampling points Apple GPUs offer, and the\n  encode path already gives every kernel its own encoder), ticks\n  scaled onto the buffer''s own GPUStartTime→GPUEndTime residency —\n  self-calibrating, no CPU/GPU clock correlation. The solo relaunch\n  of run_each_timed (sync-floored sums) becomes the fallback for\n  devices without counter sampling. llama: 23.7ms wall vs Σ kernels\n  19.4ms — the ~15% of a step spent in inter-encoder bubbles is\n  visible for the first time.\n- kernel entry names say what a kernel computes: tinygrad''s\n  kind+loop-structure names, with sanic''s named axes —\n  fold_singleton1_kv_projection512_over_hidden2048. Isomorphic stages\n  compose the same name and dedup into one entry point; distinct\n  kernels that collide number _2, _3…, and the bindless Args_ struct\n  renames with them (two wide kernels sharing one struct definition\n  was a real MSL compile break). Bindless isomorphic kernels can now\n  dedup at all — their Args_k_tN names used to block canonical\n  equality.\n- launches print CUDA-style: grid=(g,1,1) block=(b,1,1); one rule,\n  Dispatch::threadgroup_threads, shared by encode, the ICB capture,\n  and the dumps.\n- a gather''s table traffic is statically output volume × element\n  width (each output element loads exactly ONE table element), so the\n  embedding lookup stops being charged its whole 525MB table: the\n  step footer''s DRAM position is honest now, ~3014MB → ~2488MB.\n- the debug_bar histogram column is gone (the % column and the ranked\n  footer already carry it); stage_plans shrinks to the fused costs\n  the planner chose by.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"384845152717f84b9e81130a6b98b098d31a6c79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/384845152717f84b9e81130a6b98b098d31a6c79"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/90451e65d6bd6d11852b792f957c0e51fc8885f5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/90451e65d6bd6d11852b792f957c0e51fc8885f5","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDkwNDUxZTY1ZDZiZDZkMTE4NTJiNzkyZjk1N2MwZTUxZmM4ODg1ZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/70d32bdfca61a1468515d42ac60a1d74f284af75","sha":"70d32bdfca61a1468515d42ac60a1d74f284af75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/70d32bdfca61a1468515d42ac60a1d74f284af75"}],"sha":"90451e65d6bd6d11852b792f957c0e51fc8885f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/90451e65d6bd6d11852b792f957c0e51fc8885f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/70d32bdfca61a1468515d42ac60a1d74f284af75/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T20:23:39Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T20:23:39Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"the library face and the cost model''s synthesis groundwork\n\nSquash of eight steps:\n- boundary storage is a policy: bf16 intermediates, f32 accumulators\n- the library face: Tensor, named dimensions, nn::ops, stateful Graph\n- llama is a library consumer now\n- cargo fmt\n- two stated rules the roofline cannot price: chunk everywhere, lanes over rows\n- mem_occupancy learns Little''s law: bytes in flight, not lane count\n- gradient is a query: node targets, stop boundaries, pruned paths, fair ties\n- stored(dtype): a boundary''s rounding is a value, not a schedule side effect","tree":{"sha":"d2f0b8ab534853540395cfc26e2ba6388bae068f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/d2f0b8ab534853540395cfc26e2ba6388bae068f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/70d32bdfca61a1468515d42ac60a1d74f284af75","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/70d32bdfca61a1468515d42ac60a1d74f284af75","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDcwZDMyYmRmY2E2MWExNDY4NTE1ZDQyYWM2MGExZDc0ZjI4NGFmNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/c79489159494af5e9010625c4737e2413ca656c5","sha":"c79489159494af5e9010625c4737e2413ca656c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/c79489159494af5e9010625c4737e2413ca656c5"}],"sha":"70d32bdfca61a1468515d42ac60a1d74f284af75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/70d32bdfca61a1468515d42ac60a1d74f284af75"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/c79489159494af5e9010625c4737e2413ca656c5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T18:56:05Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T18:56:27Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"hold the token stream while debug lines own the terminal\n\nSANIC_DEBUG>=2 prints one stderr line per step; streaming token pieces\nto stdout mid-line spliced the two. Under debug the example now holds\nthe text and prints it once after generation; without debug it streams\nexactly as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"921b7a3772fb49eb8b060764e30ec08e8da79771","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/921b7a3772fb49eb8b060764e30ec08e8da79771"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/c79489159494af5e9010625c4737e2413ca656c5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/c79489159494af5e9010625c4737e2413ca656c5","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGM3OTQ4OTE1OTQ5NGFmNWU5MDEwNjI1YzQ3MzdlMjQxM2NhNjU2YzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/ea4dac2dd16346374eb8e302fbea34a73ebe8779","sha":"ea4dac2dd16346374eb8e302fbea34a73ebe8779","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/ea4dac2dd16346374eb8e302fbea34a73ebe8779"}],"sha":"c79489159494af5e9010625c4737e2413ca656c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/c79489159494af5e9010625c4737e2413ca656c5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/ea4dac2dd16346374eb8e302fbea34a73ebe8779/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T18:38:23Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T18:38:23Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"runtime debug tells the truth per step: real graph time at DEBUG=2\n\ntinygrad''s display trade adopted: never break the batch to observe it.\n\n- SANIC_DEBUG=2 now prints one line per replayed graph with the REAL\n  command-buffer time (GPUEndTime - GPUStartTime of the intact step),\n  the whole step against the plan''s fold total, and the aggregate DRAM\n  position. Warm-up and preemption show up as what they are.\n- SANIC_DEBUG=3 additionally dumps each frozen graph once: execution\n  order, kind, grid, planned cost and share. Plan-side only — Metal has\n  no per-kernel time inside one command buffer and we do not fake one\n  (tinygrad''s Metal PROFILE evenly spaces kernels across the interval;\n  declined).\n- The old per-kernel measured dump moves to SANIC_DEBUG=4, labeled for\n  what it is: each kernel re-run SOLO in its own command buffer —\n  accurate per launch, a different execution regime, sync-floored in\n  sum.\n- Replay command buffers are setLabel''d (\"sanic batched N\") so steps\n  are named in Instruments/Xcode GPU captures.\n\nllama @ ctx16, DEBUG=2: batched 263, 28.1ms GPU steady-state,\nvs plan Σ ×1.79, ~3013MB at 53% of peak bandwidth per step.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9f5194355675b2c2c082b32c2717aed21c6313b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/9f5194355675b2c2c082b32c2717aed21c6313b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/ea4dac2dd16346374eb8e302fbea34a73ebe8779","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/ea4dac2dd16346374eb8e302fbea34a73ebe8779","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGVhNGRhYzJkZDE2MzQ2Mzc0ZWI4ZTMwMmZiZWEzNGE3M2ViZTg3Nzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/3e868865f868cfd0276e5bb956e1ded4edbcb9ac","sha":"3e868865f868cfd0276e5bb956e1ded4edbcb9ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/3e868865f868cfd0276e5bb956e1ded4edbcb9ac"}],"sha":"ea4dac2dd16346374eb8e302fbea34a73ebe8779","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/ea4dac2dd16346374eb8e302fbea34a73ebe8779"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/3e868865f868cfd0276e5bb956e1ded4edbcb9ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T17:59:03Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T17:59:03Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"one resolver spans a walk: compile drops 54.5s -> 4.6s\n\nTwo sites recomputed axis resolution against a FRESH memo per visited\nnode, so a single call was quadratic in graph depth:\n\n- all_axis_refs::walk called the free axis_refs(node) at every node\n  (the site behind derive''s descendant_axis, whose own comment warned\n  about exactly this cost);\n- count_flops'' per-node volume cache called free axis_refs(n) per\n  MISS, so each cached volume still paid a whole-subtree resolve.\n\nBoth now thread one Resolver through the walk, the same fix the alias\nwalk got in 4339843. Measured on the llama example, identical command,\nctx 16: compile 54.5s -> 14.8s (all_axis_refs) -> 4.6s (count_flops),\n327 kernels and token-identical output at every step, decode tok/s\nunchanged. The old pre-frontier-fix best was 11s.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"099d3773d8d567eeddb17fcf622a5c459ec989f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/099d3773d8d567eeddb17fcf622a5c459ec989f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/3e868865f868cfd0276e5bb956e1ded4edbcb9ac","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/3e868865f868cfd0276e5bb956e1ded4edbcb9ac","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDNlODY4ODY1Zjg2OGNmZDAyNzZlNWJiOTU2ZTFkZWQ0ZWRiY2I5YWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/ea0d9b244a2ce9a744d815e736d8ebb6d94e17c6","sha":"ea0d9b244a2ce9a744d815e736d8ebb6d94e17c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/ea0d9b244a2ce9a744d815e736d8ebb6d94e17c6"}],"sha":"3e868865f868cfd0276e5bb956e1ded4edbcb9ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/3e868865f868cfd0276e5bb956e1ded4edbcb9ac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/ea0d9b244a2ce9a744d815e736d8ebb6d94e17c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T08:43:40Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T08:43:40Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"constructors intern: one weak table replaces three dedup boundaries\n\nEvery ir constructor now returns THE node for its shallow structure,\nfrom a global sharded weak table; Node::drop evicts its own entry (the\neviction is pointer-guarded, so a racing constructor that replaced a\ndead entry is never clobbered). Structural identity is pointer identity\nfrom birth, not downstream of a pass.\n\nDeleted as redundant: the pipeline-entry canonicalize_many, the\npartitioner''s Canonicalizer (entry tree walk + every canon.shallow on\nsplice/rebuild paths), and simplify''s per-pass CSE table. The\npointer-keyed keepalives stay: a pass cache keyed by raw address still\nmust pin its nodes against allocator reuse — interning dedups\nstructure, it does not stop a DIFFERENT structure landing on a dead\nnode''s address.\n\nMeasured on the llama example, identical command, ctx 16: compile\n54.3s -> 54.5s, 327 kernels, token-identical output, decode tok/s\nwithin noise. This is consolidation, not speed: one mechanism where\nthere were three, and pins in tests/tensor.rs + tests/simplify.rs\nflipped to the new law (identical construction IS one node).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f1b63df332b6775c7c3db4465566600977435edb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/f1b63df332b6775c7c3db4465566600977435edb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/ea0d9b244a2ce9a744d815e736d8ebb6d94e17c6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/ea0d9b244a2ce9a744d815e736d8ebb6d94e17c6","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGVhMGQ5YjI0NGEyY2U5YTc0NGQ4MTVlNzM2ZDhlYmI2ZDk0ZTE3YzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/a213c3d7661b3177b51423a00a66a902d0983dc4","sha":"a213c3d7661b3177b51423a00a66a902d0983dc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/a213c3d7661b3177b51423a00a66a902d0983dc4"}],"sha":"ea0d9b244a2ce9a744d815e736d8ebb6d94e17c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/ea0d9b244a2ce9a744d815e736d8ebb6d94e17c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/a213c3d7661b3177b51423a00a66a902d0983dc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T08:29:12Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T08:29:12Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"NodeRef goes atomic: Rc -> Arc, and the tax is noise\n\nPrerequisite for constructor interning: a global weak table needs\nSend + Sync node handles. Mechanical swap everywhere a refcount holds\na Node; pass-local caches that never cross a thread keep Rc (interp\nvalues, verify shapes, the Resolver''s shape/axis memos).\n\nMeasured on the llama example, identical command, ctx 16: compile\n55.3s -> 54.3s, 327 kernels and token-identical output both sides,\ndecode 34.1 -> 34.0 tok/s, replay 28.3 ms/tok unchanged. Refcount\ntraffic is not where compile time lives.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2748ac8de8377acfcd6535ea5f5d588a250b0945","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/2748ac8de8377acfcd6535ea5f5d588a250b0945"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/a213c3d7661b3177b51423a00a66a902d0983dc4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/a213c3d7661b3177b51423a00a66a902d0983dc4","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGEyMTNjM2Q3NjYxYjMxNzdiNTE0MjNhMDBhNjZhOTAyZDA5ODNkYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/be00679cef9178abc4f2dc5e2fa6881ad86d12f7","sha":"be00679cef9178abc4f2dc5e2fa6881ad86d12f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/be00679cef9178abc4f2dc5e2fa6881ad86d12f7"}],"sha":"a213c3d7661b3177b51423a00a66a902d0983dc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/a213c3d7661b3177b51423a00a66a902d0983dc4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/be00679cef9178abc4f2dc5e2fa6881ad86d12f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T08:16:51Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T08:16:51Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"price recomputation at cut time; retire the defer-div rule (Prop 4.1)\n\n- leaf_cuts'' cheap-op / stream-invariance gates become the Prop 4.1\n  per-thread cover inequality (inline_pays): (m-1)(w/pi + reads/beta) <\n  (m+1)|T|/beta + lambda, with m = out_vol*K/|u| and a SIMD lane-share\n  discount on output axes the carrier already shares across a lane.\n- a committed spec''s cost is best_fold_sched''s ADDITIVE time and its\n  execution flop bill, recompute included (kernel_time_additive, the\n  theory-8 factor-2 surrogate): a roofline max ties fusions doing\n  strictly more work under the same traffic. The max stays the model\n  for cooperative tiled searches (flash client pins it).\n- the defer-div scheduling exclusion is deleted; emit_fold prices\n  fused vs cut-at-divisor directly, with the divisor subtree''s own\n  work in the cut''s floor so flash''s o/l never prices as a free cut.\n  SANIC_DEBUG=3 prints each [div-cut?] decision.\n- oracle: committed costs must band measurement (measured <= 8x plan,\n  plan <= 32x measured, tests/metal.rs); norm-into-fat-head pins the\n  priced split on m1_pro (on toy the same fusion legitimately fuses --\n  the rule is the price, not the shape). The unmeasured silu pin is\n  overturned: the activation cone materializes, matching the measured\n  Trinity twin.\n\nllama @ ctx16: 311 -> 263 kernels; ctx38 A/B: 32.4 -> 33.2 tok/s,\ntoken-identical output; plan-vs-measured total x0.22 -> x1.56.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"80cb8b3fb0b77990f943bac3489f9f02da492491","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/80cb8b3fb0b77990f943bac3489f9f02da492491"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/be00679cef9178abc4f2dc5e2fa6881ad86d12f7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/be00679cef9178abc4f2dc5e2fa6881ad86d12f7","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGJlMDA2NzljZWY5MTc4YWJjNGYyZGM1ZTJmYTY4ODFhZDg2ZDEyZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/4339843d84072e51af962f8abcbccd37d1feaac0","sha":"4339843d84072e51af962f8abcbccd37d1feaac0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/4339843d84072e51af962f8abcbccd37d1feaac0"}],"sha":"be00679cef9178abc4f2dc5e2fa6881ad86d12f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/be00679cef9178abc4f2dc5e2fa6881ad86d12f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/4339843d84072e51af962f8abcbccd37d1feaac0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T01:21:50Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T01:21:50Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"share the positional resolver with the alias walk\n\nThe compile-time regression that arrived with the reindex identity law\n(41s -> 98s on the 16-layer decode graph) profiled to one site:\naxis_aliases walked the cone calling the UNCACHED axis_refs per node.\nBefore the identity law a reindex was a recursion barrier for occurrence\nresolution, which kept each fresh-resolver call shallow; pass-through\nidentity now resolves through every RoPE flip and GQA repeat down the\nwhole residual history, so per-call resolution went O(depth) and the\nalias walk O(depth^2).\n\nThe alias walk now uses the same resolver the structure cache already\nowns, so occurrence and shape resolution are memoized across every\nderivation of one compile: 98s -> 54s, schedules byte-identical. The\nresolver pins every node it answers for -- its tables are keyed by raw\npointer, and a dropped transient''s address could otherwise be reused by\na new node and answered with the stale entry.\n\nMeasured while verifying: the kernel count is context-length dependent\n(311 at 16 reserved slots, 247 at 7) -- the extent-capped slab pricing\nadmits more fusion at shorter contexts. Expected behavior of 8289b42,\nrecorded here so the varying count is not mistaken for nondeterminism.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"57f8a255ae6509c6a24e22e3bb8c32cb9343d4b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/57f8a255ae6509c6a24e22e3bb8c32cb9343d4b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/4339843d84072e51af962f8abcbccd37d1feaac0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/4339843d84072e51af962f8abcbccd37d1feaac0","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDQzMzk4NDNkODQwNzJlNTFhZjk2MmY4YWJjYmNjZDM3ZDFmZWFhYzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/8289b42a0fadaeb3a00badf58aef3ac99db91131","sha":"8289b42a0fadaeb3a00badf58aef3ac99db91131","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/8289b42a0fadaeb3a00badf58aef3ac99db91131"}],"sha":"4339843d84072e51af962f8abcbccd37d1feaac0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/4339843d84072e51af962f8abcbccd37d1feaac0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/8289b42a0fadaeb3a00badf58aef3ac99db91131/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T21:53:42Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T21:53:42Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"price streamed slabs and flatten-group shares honestly\n\nTwo cost-model corrections, one measured boundary recorded:\n\n- A streamed slab never exceeds the axis itself: TILE_N capped by the\n  streamed extent, so a 7-token KV cache is not priced as a 64-element\n  slab.\n- An input axis reaching a scheduled axis through a flatten group (GQA:\n  the key cache''s kv_heads inside the group that forms query_heads) is\n  coupled to it: a block covering a tile of the group touches the\n  proportional share of the member, not its whole extent — in SRAM and\n  in the re-read factors. Group membership is collected once per compile\n  (GroupCache, threaded through partition like the structure cache).\n\nThe defer-div scheduling exclusion stays, now with its real reason\nmeasured and written down: lifting it lets the planner fuse the RMSNorm\nvocab head (128k outputs, 15× worse than planned) and the residual-\nhistory projections, taking llama decode from 28.6 to 141 ms/tok at 181\nkernels — fewer launches, far more per-point recompute, exactly Law 3''s\ntraffic-not-launches. The exclusion lifts when leaf cutting prices\nrecomputation (Prop 4.1) so the roofline can reject those fusions on\ncost. With it in place llama holds 311 kernels at 28.0 ms/tok, all\ncorrect.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"19f9fa961cb73a68dfedd0496a1b7a54255aae32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/19f9fa961cb73a68dfedd0496a1b7a54255aae32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/8289b42a0fadaeb3a00badf58aef3ac99db91131","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/8289b42a0fadaeb3a00badf58aef3ac99db91131","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDgyODliNDJhMGZhZGFlYjNhMDBiYWRmNThhZWYzYWM5OWRiOTExMzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/67dcc179422d01e98bb0e8f88f13fa53ee3c7b8d","sha":"67dcc179422d01e98bb0e8f88f13fa53ee3c7b8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/67dcc179422d01e98bb0e8f88f13fa53ee3c7b8d"}],"sha":"8289b42a0fadaeb3a00badf58aef3ac99db91131","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/8289b42a0fadaeb3a00badf58aef3ac99db91131"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/67dcc179422d01e98bb0e8f88f13fa53ee3c7b8d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T21:03:27Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T21:03:27Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"a reindex acts only on the dimensions it transforms\n\nAxis occurrences made every reindex output dimension fresh, even one the\nmap passes through with a single coefficient-1, offset-0 term and an\nunchanged descriptor — while the view arm already preserved 1:1\nidentities. The inconsistency broke the general law that folding over an\naxis commutes with reindexing of the OTHER axes: a coupled (max, Σexp)\ncarrier declined through any free-axis broadcast, because the running\nmax''s reduction no longer matched the streamed occurrence and the whole\ncone classified free. The GQA head repeat was the instance that surfaced\nit; nothing in the fix names attention.\n\nUntransformed dimensions now keep their source occurrence, the same rule\nthe view arm applies. The full GQA + computed-mask decode attention cone\nderives the (m, l, o) flash carrier, pinned as a carrier law\n(coupled_carrier_composes_through_free_axis_repeat) with the theory doc''s\nAppendix B.2 updated to record the resolution.\n\nAt compact extents the compiled schedule now fuses whole-attention into\none kernel and defers RMS normalizers into their consuming projections.\nThe llama schedule is unchanged (311 kernels, output identical): its\nfused cone derives but plan_axis finds no feasible block structure at 32\nheads x 64 head_dim and carves the softmax division back out — the\nblocker moved from the algebra (§5) to the tiling search (§3), which is\nthe next piece of work.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a915160bba2c7836a9cb97aecccfb510f71ef24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/2a915160bba2c7836a9cb97aecccfb510f71ef24"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/67dcc179422d01e98bb0e8f88f13fa53ee3c7b8d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/67dcc179422d01e98bb0e8f88f13fa53ee3c7b8d","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDY3ZGNjMTc5NDIyZDAxZTk4YmIwZThmODhmMTNmYTUzZWUzYzdiOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/ad53dc17ea8cc2cb5024045e5f462df939ba6cfe","sha":"ad53dc17ea8cc2cb5024045e5f462df939ba6cfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/ad53dc17ea8cc2cb5024045e5f462df939ba6cfe"}],"sha":"67dcc179422d01e98bb0e8f88f13fa53ee3c7b8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/67dcc179422d01e98bb0e8f88f13fa53ee3c7b8d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/ad53dc17ea8cc2cb5024045e5f462df939ba6cfe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T20:36:05Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T20:36:05Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"test the decision-loop claims; erratum: widening is not monotone\n\nkernel_fusion_theory.md §6 prescribes sliding the cut as the missing\nanalysis behind the decode graph''s 5-kernel attention. Verify its three\nload-bearing claims against the implementation (tests/theory_check.rs,\nfindings recorded as Appendix B):\n\n- The widened masked decode cone — iota/position mask, softmax, ·V —\n  derives the 3-slot (m, ℓ, o) carrier in one query and its single kernel\n  matches the interpreter at 5e-8. The claim holds as stated; only the\n  narrow cut is ever offered today, and no decline records that.\n- The GQA head repeat is the decline that keeps the llama graph''s widest\n  derivable cut at the materialized scores: same cone, grouped-query\n  broadcast added, declines at the normalizer sum. Semantically the repeat\n  acts on a free axis, so this is a named F_syn gap with §5.5''s two\n  remediations open.\n- \"Widening past a linear consumer can only shrink the Nerode dimension\"\n  is FALSE as stated: a linear consumer that merges a sibling branch of\n  the same stream yields the product carrier, and Σx widened past\n  Add(·, Σ i·x) measures dimension 1 -> 2. §6 now states the frontier-only\n  condition and demotes early exit to a safe heuristic. The counterexample\n  also exposes a rank-harness caveat: fixed-length prefixes hide\n  position-carrying state behind column centering, so futures matrices\n  must mix prefix lengths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a9d09f6a20bcba58f19e09d471da918c8225eff9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/a9d09f6a20bcba58f19e09d471da918c8225eff9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/ad53dc17ea8cc2cb5024045e5f462df939ba6cfe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/ad53dc17ea8cc2cb5024045e5f462df939ba6cfe","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGFkNTNkYzE3ZWE4Y2MyY2I1MDI0MDQ1ZTVmNDYyZGY5MzliYTZjZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/1977a7e7d0555fad4d5e361e3ee376507992956e","sha":"1977a7e7d0555fad4d5e361e3ee376507992956e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/1977a7e7d0555fad4d5e361e3ee376507992956e"}],"sha":"ad53dc17ea8cc2cb5024045e5f462df939ba6cfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/ad53dc17ea8cc2cb5024045e5f462df939ba6cfe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/1977a7e7d0555fad4d5e361e3ee376507992956e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T19:17:00Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T19:17:00Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"guard the rescale merge at -inf; make test oracles NaN-honest\n\nThe ExpShifted combine computed each side''s weight as exp(m − M). When a\npartial''s max is −∞ — the identity accumulator of a lane that folded only\nsoftmax-masked elements — and M is also −∞, that factor is exp(−∞ − −∞) =\nNaN. Any split of a prefix-masked flash fold whose visible prefix is\nshorter than the split width hits this: decode attention NaN''d on every\nprefill step once the KV extent crossed the lane width, which the fold\nfrontier fix newly exposed by letting those folds derive split schedules.\nThe factor for a −∞ side is now forced to zero, which makes the carrier\nidentity absorbing under the merge for every split shape.\n\nThe regression was invisible to the whole suite because every\nmax-accumulating oracle folded errors with f64::max, and\nf64::max(0, NaN) = 0 — an all-NaN GPU result reported as ZERO error.\nError folds now use total_cmp so NaN ranks worst and fails the tolerance\nassert; the generated Rust harnesses in decode/rustgen get the same fix.\nWith honest oracles the new short-prefix lane-split flash test goes\nNaN-red without the guard and passes at 4.2e-8 with it.\n\nLlama 3.2 1B generates correctly again at every -n (33.4 decode tok/s);\nstep-2 logits match the MLX fp32 reference to ~1e-5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe280759f250f7682858550e260da5bc5b99ca96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/fe280759f250f7682858550e260da5bc5b99ca96"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/1977a7e7d0555fad4d5e361e3ee376507992956e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/1977a7e7d0555fad4d5e361e3ee376507992956e","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDE5NzdhN2U3ZDA1NTVmYWQ0ZDVlMzYxZTNlZTM3NjUwNzk5Mjk1NmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/0813ce3a83a93cc85464f30b34f79c11bd9d825d","sha":"0813ce3a83a93cc85464f30b34f79c11bd9d825d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/0813ce3a83a93cc85464f30b34f79c11bd9d825d"}],"sha":"1977a7e7d0555fad4d5e361e3ee376507992956e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/1977a7e7d0555fad4d5e361e3ee376507992956e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/0813ce3a83a93cc85464f30b34f79c11bd9d825d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T18:56:43Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T18:56:43Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"stop the fold frontier at materialized producers\n\nbest_fold vetted each candidate axis by testing membership of its ORIGINAL\noccurrence in the axis refs of the SPLICED graph. Splicing replaces a\nmaterialized producer with a buffer read that owns fresh occurrences, so\nany reduction whose axis was owned by a node inside that producer failed\nthe check and was silently dropped — no derive attempt, no recorded\ndecline — and partition emitted it as a scalar fallback reading a buffer\nthat a just-emitted map had materialized. Layer 0 of a transformer always\nderived (its occurrences are owned by graph inputs, which splicing\npreserves); every deeper layer hit the mismatch, which is why the llama\nschedule carried 190 map+fallback pairs that the decline census never saw.\n\nThe frontier walk now stops at nodes the partitioner has already\nmaterialized — a done producer is a buffer read, not part of this stage —\nwhich answers the question in the space it is asked in, and the spliced\nlive-set check is deleted.\n\nLlama 3.2 1B: 487 -> 311 kernels, zero fallbacks, decode 4.95 -> 30.3\ntok/s (200 -> 28 ms/tok replayed), output unchanged and still matching the\nMLX fp32 reference. The compact two-layer oracle drops 63 -> 27 kernels\nand the toy transformer block partitions to 9 kernels, all folds, which\nmoves that test''s multi-kernel floor from 10 to 2. Compile time pays for\nthe deeper derives: 11s -> 41s on the 16-layer graph.\n\nThe schedule dump now also prints the decline census, so a workload''s\ndeclines are visible exactly where its kernels are.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"27f64da6c9684fe706e33c5edfd84026af4a8a71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/27f64da6c9684fe706e33c5edfd84026af4a8a71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/0813ce3a83a93cc85464f30b34f79c11bd9d825d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/0813ce3a83a93cc85464f30b34f79c11bd9d825d","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKDA4MTNjZTNhODNhOTNjYzg1NDY0ZjMwYjM0Zjc5YzExYmQ5ZDgyNWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/d95d079b1e645f10f40aef3a529c4c8f063196d6","sha":"d95d079b1e645f10f40aef3a529c4c8f063196d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/d95d079b1e645f10f40aef3a529c4c8f063196d6"}],"sha":"0813ce3a83a93cc85464f30b34f79c11bd9d825d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/0813ce3a83a93cc85464f30b34f79c11bd9d825d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/d95d079b1e645f10f40aef3a529c4c8f063196d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T05:45:27Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T05:45:27Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"restore the clean clippy gate on Rust 1.94\n\nRust 1.94 started flagging hundreds of needless borrows across the tree;\napply its mechanical fixes. Name the resolved affine reindex row\n(ResolvedAffineIndex) and use the existing AffineIndex alias at the\nsignatures that spelled the tuple out, which also settles the type\ncomplexity lints.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1cb2372df5eaeda104a5d3add53fd3fd041c8fd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/1cb2372df5eaeda104a5d3add53fd3fd041c8fd1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/d95d079b1e645f10f40aef3a529c4c8f063196d6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/d95d079b1e645f10f40aef3a529c4c8f063196d6","node_id":"C_kwDOTBf03doAKGQ5NWQwNzliMWU2NDVmMTBmNDBhZWYzYTUyOWM0YzhmMDYzMTk2ZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe/sanic/commit/190867dfe6412d8feb05f743ac1314c865472019","sha":"190867dfe6412d8feb05f743ac1314c865472019","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/190867dfe6412d8feb05f743ac1314c865472019"}],"sha":"d95d079b1e645f10f40aef3a529c4c8f063196d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/d95d079b1e645f10f40aef3a529c4c8f063196d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/commits/190867dfe6412d8feb05f743ac1314c865472019/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T05:41:32Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T05:41:32Z","email":"leo.paille@enseirb-matmeca.fr","name":"Léo Paillé"},"message":"fix Metal fast math deleting -inf softmax masks\n\nMetal''s default compile options enable fast math, which assumes no ±inf\never occurs and constant-folds the additive attention mask\nscore + (visible ? 0 : -INFINITY) down to score. Every reserved KV-cache\nslot then leaked exp(0) into the softmax denominator, so Llama''s logits\ndepended on the reserved context length (-n) and diverged from the fp32\nreference. A mask bound as an input buffer is runtime data the compiler\ncannot fold, which is why the existing masked-attention GPU tests passed.\n\nCompile shaders with MTLMathModeRelaxed: value optimizations stay, inf/nan\nsemantics return, and decode timing is unchanged (199.6 vs 199.5 ms/tok).\n\nLlama 3.2 1B now generates token-for-token identically to the MLX fp32\nreference (\"Paris. It is the most populous city in France\"), with step-0\nlogits bit-identical across -n 3/10/16 and matching MLX f32 to ~1e-5.\nThe earlier \"Paris. The\" reference text is MLX''s own bf16 rounding: in\nbf16 the top two logits quantize to exactly 21.625 and argmax breaks the\ntie by index.\n\nTwo regressions pin this: a minimal fused attention whose mask is computed\nfrom iota and a runtime position scalar, and a compact two-layer GQA decode\nprefilled at four reserved extents, checking Metal against the interpreter\non every root of every step and the interpreter against itself across\nextents.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6555c980fcb99369083f9ae33137361f9ffc215f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/trees/6555c980fcb99369083f9ae33137361f9ffc215f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Leikoe/sanic/git/commits/190867dfe6412d8feb05f743ac1314c865472019","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44068562?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leikoe","id":44068562,"login":"Leikoe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDY4NTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leikoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users