i-sketch","node_id":"U_kgDOEH6eFg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codeshivamsi-sketch/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codeshivamsi-sketch/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codeshivamsi-sketch/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codeshivamsi-sketch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codeshivamsi-sketch/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codeshivamsi-sketch","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codeshivamsi-sketch/ai_study_assistant_edumind/commits/4036e8e34630d9934c43ffa616cc107adbd09e96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T19:19:08Z","email":"code.shivam.si@gmail.com","name":"codeshivamsi-sketch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T19:19:08Z","email":"code.shivam.si@gmail.com","name":"codeshivamsi-sketch"},"message":"fix: baseline notifications'' Prisma migration, fix retry test''s worker\n\nnotifications was crash-looping on P3005 (\"schema not empty\") - a\n00000000000000_baseline no-op migration already existed to reconcile\nAlembic''s pre-existing tables, but the startup command never actually\nresolved it, so `prisma migrate deploy` refused to run against the\nshared edumind database. Resolve the baseline first (idempotent via\n`|| true`), then deploy as before.\n\ntest_notify_quiz_ready_retries_then_fails expected a worker consuming\nits own queue with a fast retry countdown - no such worker existed, so\nit just timed out. Add a conftest.py fixture that spawns one. Its\nretry-then-fail path also turns out to have been passing only because\nnotifications was down; point it at a guaranteed-closed port instead\nso the failure is deterministic rather than incidental.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7a15fef22162d1f6010f87d1547afbca7b4c9947","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codeshivamsi-ske